      "name": "ProcessCleanupContext",
      "signature": "void ProcessCleanupContext(GameDataCollection * pCleanupContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Performs complete cleanup and resource deallocation for a game data collection context.\nThis function systematically processes and cleans up various types of game resources stored\nin the GameDataCollection structure to prevent memory leaks and properly release handles.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Reset cleanup flags by clearing offset 0x10 to signal processing has started\n2. Process active items with stored callback while count > 0:\n   - Load active count from offset 0xc and check if positive\n   - Call FUN_6fadc380 with (base_pointer + count) as parameter for cleanup\n   - Continue loop until no active items remain (count becomes 0 or negative)\n3. Process array elements if array exists (count > 0):\n   - Check array element count at offset 0x18 for non-zero value\n   - Initialize loop variables for array traversal\n   - For each array element using 12-byte stride pattern:\n     - Load resource handle from array_base + element_offset + 8\n     - Call stored callback function pointer from offset 0x0 with handle\n     - Advance to next element by adding 0xc bytes to offset\n   - Continue until all array elements processed\n4. Clean up hash object resources (type 1 resources):\n   - Load resource handle from offset 0x40 and check if positive\n   - Call FUN_6fadc7c0 for hash object destruction and cleanup\n   - Call Ordinal_403 with hash object debug identifier string\n   - Repeat loop until no more type 1 resources remain\n5. Clean up game data resources (type 2 resources):\n   - Load resource handle from offset 0x30 and check if positive\n   - Call FUN_6fadc310 for game data destruction and cleanup\n   - Call Ordinal_403 with game data debug identifier string\n   - Repeat loop until no more type 2 resources remain\n\nParameters:\n  pCleanupContext (GameDataCollection *) - Pointer to game data collection structure containing:\n    - Function pointer for array element cleanup callbacks\n    - Active item data pointers and counts for processing\n    - Array of elements requiring individual cleanup operations\n    - Resource handles for different cleanup types (hash objects, game data)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, performs cleanup operations through side effects only\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If no active items (count <= 0), skips directly to array processing phase\n  - If no array elements (count = 0), skips array processing and moves to resource cleanup\n  - Resource cleanup loops continue until all handles are exhausted or become invalid\n  - Debug strings in Ordinal_403 calls identify resource types during cleanup operations",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
