      "name": "InsertListNode",
      "signature": "void InsertListNode(void * this, int param_1, int param_2, uint param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Inserts a node into a doubly-linked list at head or tail position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate node structure via SMemAlloc (Ordinal_401) with size = nInsertMode + 0x38 bytes\n2. Initialize node fields to zero: offsets +4, +8, +C, +10, +2C, +30, +34\n3. Set self-reference at offset +30 for list integrity validation\n4. Store inverted pointer (~pdwNode) at +34 for corruption detection\n5. If pListContainer is non-NULL, proceed with insertion:\n   a. Calculate list node pointer from container base or offset +4\n   b. If existing head node present, unlink it from current position\n   c. For head insertion (nInsertMode != 1): link before current head\n   d. For tail insertion (nInsertMode == 1): link after current tail\n\nParameters:\n  this (void*) - IMPLICIT __thiscall; container structure with list head/tail at +4/+8\n  pListContainer (void*) - NULL to skip insertion; 0x1 for tail; other for head insertion\n  nInsertMode (int) - allocation size component; also 0=skip, 1=tail, other=head\n  nNodeHeader (int) - base allocation flags (ORed with 0x8)\n  dwFlags (dword) - additional flags passed through to allocator\n\nReturns:\n  void - no return value; node inserted in-place into container list\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - SMemAlloc failure (returns 0): node insertion skipped, function returns early\n  - Negative offset values: inverted pointer representation, apply NOT to decode\n  - NULL pListContainer: bypasses all insertion logic\n\nStructure Layout (Node at nNodeHandle):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  +0x04   4     reserved1     Cleared to 0\n  +0x08   4     reserved2     Cleared to 0\n  +0x0C   4     reserved3     Cleared to 0\n  +0x10   4     reserved4     Cleared to 0\n  +0x2C   4     reserved5     Cleared to 0\n  +0x30   4     pLink         Self-reference pointer for validation\n  +0x34   4     dwInverted    Inverted pLink (~pLink) for integrity check",
