      "name": "ClearCollectionLinkedPointers",
      "signature": "void ClearCollectionLinkedPointers(GameDataCollection * pCollection)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Clears linked pointer chains within a GameDataCollection by iterating backwards through elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. While collection has elements (count > 0)\n2. Get pointer to current element at collection[count-1] offset\n3. Check if element has valid data pointer (not null)\n4. Extract offset value from element[1]\n5. If offset is negative, calculate target using bitwise NOT operation\n6. If offset is positive, calculate target using base pointer arithmetic\n7. Copy element's data pointer to calculated target location\n8. Update linked structure's offset field with current element's offset\n9. Clear current element's data pointer and offset (set to 0)\n10. Decrement count and continue with next element\n\nParameters:\npCollection (GameDataCollection *): Collection containing linked pointer elements to clear\n\nReturns:\nvoid: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Negative offset values (bit 31 set) use bitwise NOT operation for target calculation\n- Zero data pointers are skipped (already cleared elements)\n- Function processes elements in reverse order (backwards iteration)\n\nStructure Layout:\nGameDataCollection structure access pattern:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n+0x0   | 4    | pData      | void*| Base pointer to element array\n+0x8   | 4    | nCount     | int  | Current number of elements\n\nElement structure access pattern:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type | Description  \n+0x0   | 4    | pDataPointer  | void*| Linked data pointer\n+0x4   | 4    | dwOffset      | uint | Offset/address calculation value",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
