      "name": "InitializeGameDataListNode",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameDataListNode(GameDataList * pNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize a game data list node with signature and self-referencing structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate pointer to second field (offset +4 from base)\n2. Zero-initialize the next pointer field (offset +4)\n3. Zero-initialize the previous/count field (offset +8)  \n4. Set next pointer to point to itself (create self-referencing loop)\n5. Set signature field to magic value 0xDDDDDDDD (offset +0)\n6. Set checksum field to bitwise NOT of next pointer address (offset +8)\n\nParameters:\npNode - Pointer to GameDataList structure to initialize\n\nReturns:\nvoid (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe self-referencing pointer (field points to itself) indicates an empty/single-node list.\nThe bitwise NOT operation on address serves as an integrity checksum.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0xDDDDDDDD - List node signature/type identifier (likely \"dead\" marker in debug builds)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name | Type | Description\n-------|------|------------|------|------------\n+0     | 4    | dwSignature| uint | Magic signature (0xDDDDDDDD)\n+4     | 4    | pNext      | void*| Next node pointer (self-ref when empty)\n+8     | 4    | dwChecksum | uint | Integrity checksum (~address)",
