      "name": "InitializeGameDataElement",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameDataElement(GameDataElement * pGameDataElement)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize a GameDataElement structure with self-referencing pointers and integrity validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate address of second element (pGameDataElement + 1) and store in puVar1\n2. Clear second element to 0 (initialization)\n3. Clear third element to 0 (initialization)\n4. Set second element to point to itself (puVar1 = puVar1)\n5. Clear first element to 0 (initialization)\n6. Set third element to bitwise complement of second element address (~puVar1)\n\nParameters:\npGameDataElement - Pointer to uninitialized GameDataElement structure to initialize\n\nReturns:\nvoid (function modifies structure in-place)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe function creates a self-referencing pointer structure where the second element\npoints to itself and the third element contains the bitwise NOT of that address.\nThis pattern suggests integrity validation or corruption detection mechanism.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0 - Initialization value for all pointer fields before self-reference setup\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type  | Description\n+0x00  | 4    | pFirstPtr     | uint  | First pointer (initialized to 0)\n+0x04  | 4    | pSelfRef      | uint  | Self-referencing pointer \n+0x08  | 4    | dwIntegrity   | uint  | Bitwise complement of pSelfRef address",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
