      "name": "ResizeNodeContainer",
      "signature": "void ResizeNodeContainer(void * this, uint param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Resizes the node container to accommodate a new element count, handling memory allocation and element lifecycle.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare dwNewSize against current element count (offset +0x4)\n2. If shrinking: unlink excess nodes via UnlinkListNode loop\n3. If growing beyond capacity (offset +0x0):\n   a. Calculate expansion increment (auto-compute power-of-2 for small sizes, else 0x15)\n   b. Align new capacity to expansion increment via modulo\n   c. Destroy excess elements if shrinking allocated space\n   d. Attempt SMemReAlloc on existing buffer\n   e. If realloc fails: allocate new buffer, copy elements via InitializeExplicitListNode, destroy old copies, free old buffer\n4. If growing within capacity: initialize new elements via InitializeExplicitListNode\n5. Update element count at offset +0x4\n\nParameters:\n  this (NodeContainer*) - IMPLICIT via ECX. Pointer to the container being resized.\n                          Structure: +0x0=capacity, +0x4=count, +0x8=pElements, +0xC=expansionIncrement\n  dwNewSize (uint)      - Target number of elements for the container\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Container is modified in place.\n         On allocation failure, falls back to fresh allocation and element copy.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - dwNewSize <= current count with shrink: Unlinks excess nodes but keeps allocated capacity\n  - dwNewSize > capacity: Reallocates buffer, may destroy and recreate elements\n  - Expansion increment auto-computed as power-of-2 for sizes < 21, otherwise fixed at 21\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x15 (21) - Threshold for auto-increment calculation and fixed increment for large lists\n  0xC (12)  - Element size in bytes (sizeof TSExplicitListNode)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
