      "name": "InitializeExplicitListNode",
      "signature": "void InitializeExplicitListNode(dword * pNode, dword * pSourceNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes a TSExplicitListNode with proper linked list structure and pointer validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input node pointer is not NULL\n2. Calculate pointer to next field (offset +4 from base)\n3. Clear next pointer and hash validation field (offsets +4 and +8)\n4. Copy data value from source node to current node (offset 0)\n5. Set self-referential next pointer for initial state\n6. Generate hash validation value as bitwise complement of next pointer address\n\nParameters:\n- pNode: Pointer to TSExplicitListNode structure to initialize (ECX register)\n- pSourceNode: Pointer to source node containing data value to copy (EDX register)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pNode is NULL, function returns immediately without operation\n- Hash validation field uses bitwise NOT of next pointer address for integrity checking\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset | Size | Field Name      | Type    | Description\n0x00   | 4    | dwData          | dword   | Primary data value copied from source\n0x04   | 4    | pNext           | dword * | Pointer to next node (self-referential initially)\n0x08   | 4    | dwHashCheck     | dword   | Validation hash (~next_pointer_address)",
