      "name": "DecompressSpriteFrame",
      "signature": "void DecompressSpriteFrame(uint * pBuffer, undefined * pUnknown1, int nDataSize, int * pSpriteData, int nFrameOffset, int nStartDir, int nEndDir, int * pPixelCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint *",
      "comment": "Decompresses a sprite frame from compressed bitstream data into pixel buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section to protect shared sprite resources\n2. Allocate temporary decompression buffer from tracked memory pool\n3. Calculate direction range and frame offsets from sprite header\n4. For each direction in range (nStartDir to nEndDir):\n   a. Extract 28-bit cell header containing palette indices and flags\n   b. Build bit array index tables for fast bit extraction\n   c. Extract control flags to determine optional header presence\n   d. Process palette lookup table entries for color mapping\n   e. Calculate cell grid bounding box (min/max X/Y coordinates)\n   f. Initialize decompression buffer with cell dimensions\n   g. Decompress RLE-encoded cell data to intermediate buffer\n   h. Apply palette lookup to convert indices to RGB pixels\n   i. Copy decompressed pixel rows to output buffer\n5. Leave critical section and return allocated buffer pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pBuffer (uint* ECX): Output pixel buffer for decompressed sprite data\n  pbContextData (byte* EDX): Source compressed sprite data context\n  nDataSize (int): Size of compressed data in bytes\n  pSpriteData (int*): Pointer to sprite header containing frame offsets\n  nFrameOffset (int): Byte offset to target frame within sprite data\n  nStartDir (int): Starting direction index (0-7 typically)\n  nEndDir (int): Ending direction index (inclusive)\n  pPixelCount (int*): Output: total pixels decompressed\n  nHandle (int): Resource handle for error reporting\n\nReturns:\n  void - Pixel data written to pBuffer, count stored in pPixelCount\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if bit stream bounds exceeded (line 0x298)\n  - Asserts if direction out of range (line 0x366)\n  - Asserts if cell X/Y coordinates negative (lines 0x61a, 0x61b)\n  - Asserts if cell data pointer null (line 0x649)\n  - Fatal error on decompression failure (line 0x657)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x6feaf400: Critical section pointer (g_csSpriteMutex)\n  0x6fe367c8: Static pixel output buffer base address\n  0x6fe33bc8: Cell descriptor table base address\n  0x6fe2c93c: Palette index lookup table\n  0x6fe2c9fc: Bit mask lookup table (32 entries)\n  0x6fe2ca04-6c: Bit extraction masks (2,20,28 bit widths)\n  0x20: Bits per DWORD (32)\n  0x2c: Cell descriptor structure size (44 bytes)\n  0x55e: Memory pool ID for sprite decompression",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "STR",
