      "name": "ProcessBufferWithTableLookup",
      "signature": "void ProcessBufferWithTableLookup(byte * pbSource, int nDestX, int nRowCount, int nRowWidth, int nPosY, int nXMax, int nYMax, int nTableBase, int nSeed)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Applies table-based transformation to rectangular buffer region using Duff's device loop unrolling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize: Save nSeed and nPosY; calculate nRowBaseOffset = nRowWidth + nDestX\n2. For each source byte: Check sign bit (control byte if negative/0x80 set)\n   - If positive: Calculate visible range intersecting with bounds [nDestX:nXMax, nPosY:nYMax]\n   - If negative: Extract control bits and adjust position\n3. Transformation: For each visible byte, fetch source[nTableBase + byte], mix with destination byte:\n   - result = (destination << 8) + nTableSeed + table[source + nTableBase]\n   - Then extract byte from result (equivalent to XOR/mixing operation)\n4. Duff's device: Process 8 bytes per iteration in main loop, handle 0-7 remainder with switch/case\n5. Row processing: After processing all source bytes (sign change detected), move to next row\n6. Termination: When nRowCount reaches 0, return\n\nParameters:\n- pbSource (ECX): Pointer to command/source byte stream (row-major format)\n- nDestX (EDX): Initial X coordinate of destination buffer position\n- nRowCount (ESP+0x28): Number of rows to process\n- nRowWidth (ESP+0x2c): Width of each row in destination buffer\n- nPosY (ESP+0x30): Initial Y coordinate of destination buffer position\n- nXMax (ESP+0x34): Maximum X boundary (exclusive)\n- nYMax (ESP+0x38): Maximum Y boundary (exclusive)\n- nTableBase (ESP+0x3c): Base address of lookup table for source byte transformation\n- nSeed (ESP+0x40): Mixing constant for table lookups\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies destination buffer in-place)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7f: Control bit mask (lower 7 bits = magnitude, bit 7 = sign for row terminator)\n- 0x100: Multiplication factor for destination byte in mixing formula\n- 8: Duff's device stride (8-byte chunk processing)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
