      "name": "ConvertAndQuantizeRGBImage",
      "signature": "byte * ConvertAndQuantizeRGBImage(byte * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "byte *",
      "comment": "Convert RGB image to HSL color space and quantize palette\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate source palette pointer is not NULL (assert on failure)\n2. Allocate 0x6c327 bytes (442151) for output image buffer\n3. Copy source palette (0x100 entries / 256 colors) to output buffer via MOVSD.REP\n4. For each RGB pixel in source (256 total):\n   a. Extract R, G, B byte components from palette entry\n   b. Scale each component to [0.0, 1.0] range by multiplying by 1/255\n   c. Find min and max of RGB components\n   d. Calculate Lightness: L = (min + max) * 0.5\n   e. Calculate Saturation: S = (max - min) / denominator based on L\n   f. Calculate Hue: H depends on which RGB component is maximum\n   g. Store HSL triplet (24 bytes per entry) in HSL buffer\n5. For 3 color plane iterations (quantization levels):\n   a. Plane 0: blend factor 0xbf (75%), Plane 1: 0x7f (50%), Plane 2: 0x3f (25%)\n   b. For each source/target color pair, perform weighted RGB blending\n   c. Use magic divisor 0x80808081 for fast division by 255\n   d. Call FindClosestColorMatch to find nearest palette index\n   e. Store quantized indices at buffer offset 0x3500 + plane*0x10000\n6. Generate grayscale ramp palette (32 intensity levels, 256 entries each)\n7. Post-process: QuantizeColorPalette, QuantizePaletteImage, QuantizeColorTo256Palette\n8. Apply PaletteQuantizeImage with HSL buffer, build lookup table\n9. Copy 37 bytes of final palette data to buffer offset 0x6b600\n10. Build final quantization table and return buffer pointer\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT: [EBP + 0x8] - pSourcePalette (uint *) - source 256-color RGBA palette\n\nReturns:\nEAX - pbQuantizedBuffer (byte *) - pointer to quantized image buffer\n\nPhantom Variables (SSA temporaries, cannot be renamed or typed):\nqwPaletteData - SSA variable representing stack parameter access, type undefined8\n               Ghidra cannot apply type to HASH-storage SSA variables\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x6c327 - image buffer allocation size (442151 bytes)\n0x100 - palette entry count (256 colors)\n0xff - maximum RGB/HSL component value (255)\n0x80808081 - magic multiplier for fast division by 255\n0x20 - grayscale ramp level count (32 levels)\n0x3500 - intermediate quantization buffer offset\n0x6b600 - final palette copy offset within buffer\n0x18 - HSL entry size (24 bytes: H, S, L as doubles)\n\nBuffer Layout:\nOffset 0x0000 - 0x03ff: 256-entry RGBA palette (1024 bytes)\nOffset 0x0400 - 0x23ff: Grayscale ramp table (32 levels x 256 entries)\nOffset 0x3500 - 0x354ff: Plane 0 quantization (256 x 256)\nOffset 0x13500 - 0x234ff: Plane 1 quantization (256 x 256)\nOffset 0x23500 - 0x334ff: Plane 2 quantization (256 x 256)\nOffset 0x6b600 - 0x6b624: Final palette copy (37 bytes)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
