      "name": "QuantizePaletteIndex",
      "signature": "void QuantizePaletteIndex(int iPaletteDataBase)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Builds palette quantization and blend lookup tables for RGB color matching.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through 256 source palette entries (outer loop)\n2. Apply 2/3 brightness reduction to each RGB component using floor(x * 2/3)\n3. For each adjusted color, search all 256 palette entries for closest match\n4. Compute squared Euclidean distance: (dR^2 + dG^2 + dB^2)\n5. Store best-match palette index at output offset +0x6b500\n6. Build 256x256 blend table at offset +0x5b500:\n   a. For each source/dest palette pair, compute maximum RGB component\n   b. Blend colors: ((src * (255 - max)) + (dst * max)) / 255\n   c. Find closest palette match for blended color\n   d. Store blend index for fast runtime lookup\n\nParameters:\n- iPaletteDataBase (int, ECX): Base pointer to palette RGB data array\n\nReturns: void (results written to palette data structure)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x55555555: Computes floor(x * 2/3) via signed multiply/shift\n- 0x80808081: Computes x / 255 via unsigned multiply and shift by 7\n- 0x6b500: Output offset for direct palette match indices (256 bytes)\n- 0x5b500: Output offset for blend table (256x256 = 65536 bytes)\n\nStructure Layout (Palette Data):\nOffset    Size      Field           Description\n0x00      0x400     rgbEntries[256] Source palette (4 bytes per entry: R,G,B,pad)\n0x5b500   0x10000   blendTable      256x256 blend lookup table\n0x6b500   0x100     quantizedIdx    256 quantized match indices",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:a3b28e596dbc6a5ff3c10eac7f028e2c41d33bc588871eb679d316d3f3cc6092",
