      "name": "PaletteQuantizeImage",
      "signature": "void PaletteQuantizeImage(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Builds color quantization lookup tables for palette-based image processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x1C34 bytes of stack space for local arrays via AllocateStackSpace\n2. Build 9 color quantization lookup tables at various offsets from pImageData:\n   - Table at offset 0x53500: Base color mapping (256 entries)\n   - Table at offset 0x54d00: Modified saturation mapping (256 entries)\n   - Table at offset 0x56500: Enhanced saturation mapping (256 entries)\n   - Table at offset 0x57d00: Luminance-adjusted mapping (256 entries)\n   - Table at offset 0x57e00: Luminance-scaled mapping (256 entries)\n   - Table at offset 0x57f00: Conditional luminance mapping (256 entries)\n   - Table at offset 0x59800: Hue-scaled mapping (12 layers x 256 entries)\n   - Table at offset 0x5a400: RGB distance-based mapping (256 entries)\n   - Table at offset 0x5a500: Green-delta mapping (256 entries)\n   - Table at offset 0x5a600: Blue-delta mapping (256 entries)\n3. For each table, process 24 layers of 256 entries each (0x18 x 0x100)\n4. Apply floating-point color scaling using constants at 0x6fe2cb80\n5. Call QuantizeColorToRGB to convert color values to RGB triplets\n6. Find nearest palette match using squared Euclidean distance: dR^2 + dG^2 + dB^2\n\nParameters:\n  pPaletteData (ECX): BYTE * - Pointer to 256-entry source palette (768 bytes RGB)\n  pImageData (EDX): BYTE * - Pointer to destination image data buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void - Lookup tables are written directly to offsets within pImageData buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Table values are clamped when floating-point results exceed 256.0 (at 0x6fe2cb08)\n- Luminance calculations may set values to zero for underflow conditions\n- Distance calculation uses signed subtraction for negative deltas\n- byColorIndex is a decompiler phantom variable (stack temp, not persistent)\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x100 (256): Number of palette entries / table size per layer\n- 0x18 (24): Number of color layers per table\n- 0x1C34 (7220): Stack allocation size for local working arrays\n- 0x53500-0x5a600: Output table offsets in destination buffer\n- Floating-point constants at 0x6fe2cb08, 0x6fe2cb28, 0x6fe2cb30, 0x6fe2cb38,\n  0x6fe2cb48, 0x6fe2cb50, 0x6fe2cb58, 0x6fe2cb60, 0x6fe2cb68, 0x6fe2cb70,\n  0x6fe2cb78, 0x6fe2cb80 are color scaling factors\n\nCalled By: ConvertAndQuantizeRGBImage\nCalls: AllocateStackSpace, QuantizeColorToRGB, __ftol",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:82893a148568a0d04302432e447bf8576632b6d086af4711c0f095195e6e327a",
