      "name": "ProcessByteTripletsWithCallback",
      "signature": "dword ProcessByteTripletsWithCallback(byte * pbInputBuffer, byte * pbOutputBuffer, int nCount, void * pfnCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Processes byte triplets (RGB values) from input buffer through a callback function.\n\nReads groups of 3 consecutive bytes from input, optionally validates them against\nthreshold 0x0A, passes through callback (default: FindNearestPaletteColor), and\nstores single-byte results in output buffer. Used for palette color mapping.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_dwPaletteValidFlag; return 0 immediately if palette not valid\n2. Use pfnCallback if provided, otherwise default to FindNearestPaletteColor (0x6fe1b5c0)\n3. For each triplet in dwTripletCount:\n   a. Read 3 consecutive bytes (R, G, B components)\n   b. If g_fErrorHandlingDisabled set AND all 3 bytes <= 0x0A:\n      - Replace triplet with validation marker (0x04, 0x00, 0x00)\n   c. Call callback(byRed, byGreen, byBlue) via __stdcall\n   d. Store returned byte to output buffer\n4. Return 0 on completion\n\nParameters:\n  pbInputBuffer  - Pointer to source buffer containing RGB byte triplets\n  pbOutputBuffer - Pointer to destination buffer for palette indices\n  dwTripletCount - Number of triplets to process (buffer must have 3x bytes)\n  pfnCallback    - Optional callback function pointer (byte __stdcall fn(byte,byte,byte))\n                   If NULL, uses FindNearestPaletteColor as default\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 0 (success indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 immediately if g_dwPaletteValidFlag is 0 (palette not loaded)\n  - When g_fErrorHandlingDisabled is set, triplets with all bytes <= 0x0A\n    are replaced with validation marker before callback\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x0A - Threshold for low-value byte validation check\n  0x04 - Validation marker byte (replaces invalid triplet)\n  0x6fe1b5c0 - Default callback address: FindNearestPaletteColor",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:57816863f408ca4e267ce0150bb3d8d65cf4986146ee89f29d7c003ff839182d",
