      "name": "BuildAndApplyPaletteShift",
      "signature": "void BuildAndApplyPaletteShift(char * szPaletteType, int nPaletteIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Builds a palette shift file path and loads palette data into the global palette table.\n\nConstructs a file path from the palette type name by concatenating:\n  data\\\\global\\\\palette\\\\ + szPaletteType + .dat\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 260-byte buffer on stack for path construction\n2. Copy file extension \".dat\" to buffer start\n3. Append palette type name (e.g., \"act1\", \"monster\")\n4. Prepend base path \"data\\\\global\\\\palette\\\\\"\n5. Call InitializeResourceAndLock to load the file\n6. If load fails: log warning and zero-fill target palette slot\n7. If load succeeds: read file data to palette slot and validate\n\nParameters:\n  szPaletteType - Palette type name string (e.g., \"act1\", \"monster\")\n                  Passed in ECX (__fastcall convention)\n  nPaletteIndex - Index into g_aPaletteShiftData table (0-N)\n                  Passed in EDX, used to calculate slot offset\n\nReturns:\n  void - On success, palette data loaded to g_aPaletteShiftData[nPaletteIndex]\n         On failure, target slot zero-filled (safe default state)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x104 (260)  - Stack buffer size for MAX_PATH-like path string\n  0x540 (1344) - DWORD count per palette slot (5376 bytes)\n  0x1500       - Palette slot size in bytes (5376 = 256 * 21)\n  0x38 (56)    - Source line number for error logging\n\nGlobal Data:\n  0x6fe30094 - szExtension \".dat\" file extension constant\n  0x6fe30084 - szBasePath \"data\\\\global\\\\palette\\\\\" base directory\n  0x6feb6ac0 - g_aPaletteShiftData palette shift data array\n\nError Handling:\n  On file load failure, logs warning via LogPoolWarning with source file\n  info and zero-fills the target palette slot to ensure safe default state",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:587abd346d569715c4530244dae5676072d08823f02ddd72ef86f32082ac7db6",
