      "comment": "Compresses player buffer data into a compact format for storage or transmission.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate temporary compression buffer (0x128 bytes / 296 bytes) from memory pool 0x5AF\n2. Clear the buffer to zero using REP STOSD (0x16B dwords)\n3. For each player data block (up to 0xF blocks, 0x20 bytes each):\n   a. Call SearchCharInBufferWithLimit to find character boundaries (max 0x7F length)\n   b. If no match found and length is 0x7F, store single byte directly\n   c. Otherwise, call ScanStringForCharacter for detailed analysis\n   d. Store character count byte, then copy matching data bytes to compression buffer\n   e. Advance block pointers by 0x20 bytes for next iteration\n4. Calculate final compressed size (ESI - buffer start)\n5. Verify compressed size is less than 0x10000 bytes (64KB limit)\n6. Allocate final output buffer matching exact compressed size\n7. Clear and copy compressed data to final buffer via MOVSD\n8. Store buffer pointer and size in output structure, set compression flags\n9. Release temporary buffer via ReleasePoolAllocation\n\nParameters:\n   nStructure (ECX): Pointer to output structure that receives compressed data\n                     - Offset +0x08: Flags byte (OR with 0x05 to mark as compressed)\n                     - Offset +0x0A: Compressed size stored as 16-bit word\n                     - Offset +0x10: Pointer to final compressed buffer\n   szSourceBuffer (EDX): Source buffer containing raw player data\n                         - Offset +0x20: Start of first data block (32-byte aligned)\n\nReturns:\n   void - Results stored directly in nStructure fields\n\nMagic Numbers:\n   0x128 (296):  Temporary buffer allocation size\n   0x5AF:        Memory pool ID for temporary allocation\n   0x20 (32):    Player data block size in bytes\n   0x7F (127):   Maximum single-block length threshold\n   0xF (15):     Maximum number of data blocks to process\n   0x10000:      Maximum allowed compressed size (64KB)\n   0x05:         Compression flag mask for structure offset +0x08\n   0x16B (363):  Number of dwords to clear in temp buffer\n\nError Handling:\n   - FogAssert triggered if temp buffer allocation fails (source line 0x129)\n   - FogAssert triggered if compressed size >= 0x10000 (source line 0x166)\n   - FogAssert triggered if final buffer allocation fails (source line 0x16A)\n   - ReportError(-1) called on all allocation failures to terminate",
