      "name": "InitializeGridStructure",
      "signature": "void InitializeGridStructure(int pGridNode, int pSourceData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize a 256-byte grid structure by copying rows from source data in a pyramid pattern.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 256-byte buffer (0x185 = 261 bytes) via Ordinal_10042\n2. Zero-fill the entire buffer (64 dwords) using REP STOSD\n3. Copy rows from source data into grid in a specific pattern for 15 rows (0xf)\n4. Row pattern: offset starts at 0xe, stride starts at 4 bytes\n5. For rows 0-7: decrease offset by 2 bytes, increase stride by 4 bytes\n6. For rows 8-14: increase offset by 2 bytes, decrease stride by 4 bytes\n7. Each row copied using REP MOVSD (dword copy) then REP MOVSB (remaining bytes)\n8. Set result structure fields: offset 0x8 = 1, offset 0xa = 0x100, offset 0x10 = buffer pointer\n\nParameters:\n- pGridNode (ECX, int): Grid node structure pointer to update with results\n- pSourceData (EDX, const void*): Source data pointer containing rows to copy\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion failure if memory allocation fails (Ordinal_10042 returns NULL)\n- Row copying pattern creates a pyramid-shaped data layout in memory\n- Stride pattern: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 28, 24, 20, 16, 12, 8, 4, 0\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x185 (261): buffer allocation size in bytes\n- 0x40 (64): number of dwords to zero-fill\n- 0xe (14): starting row offset in source data\n- 0x20 (32): offset increment between rows in source\n- 0x8, 0xa, 0x10: offsets into result structure to store dimensions and pointer\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ScanGridForNullTerminator() - Calls this to initialize grid after validation\n- Ordinal_10042 - Allocates memory (Storm.dll ordinal)\n- FogAssertFail() - Assertion handler",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:f546f9b2d468250a5aae1d0f0c1727dc",
