      "name": "CleanupProjectNodes",
      "signature": "void CleanupProjectNodes(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cleanup Project Nodes - Traverse and deallocate linked list of project structures\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load first project node from global g_pTileHashListHead\n2. If list is empty (NULL), set global to NULL and return\n3. For each node in the linked list:\n   a. Save next node pointer (offset 0x10c) before deallocation\n   b. Call ClearTileProjectData to cleanup TileProject at offset 0x104\n   c. Clear TileProject pointer to NULL\n   d. Call ClearHashTableBuckets to deallocate hash table at offset 0x108\n   e. Clear hash table pointer to NULL\n   f. Call UpdatePaletteIndex(0x29, 0) to trigger cleanup event\n   g. Move to next node and continue loop until end of list (NULL)\n4. Set global g_pTileHashListHead to NULL to mark list as cleaned\n\nParameters:\n   None\n\nReturns:\n   void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n   - 0x29: Cleanup event code\n   - 0x104: TileProject pointer offset in ProjectNode\n   - 0x108: Hash table pointer offset in ProjectNode\n   - 0x10c: Next node pointer offset in ProjectNode\n\nRelated Functions:\n   - ClearTileProjectData() - TileProject cleanup\n   - ClearHashTableBuckets() - Hash table deallocation\n   - UpdatePaletteIndex() - Cleanup event handler",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:79b8f2f6bcc8acc0e8558f8d718e2c5b8c3e73b395783016f15b172567d7a98a",
