      "name": "ExceptionHandler_Wrapper",
      "signature": "dword ExceptionHandler_Wrapper(PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord, PVOID pContext, DWORD dwExceptionFlags, dword dwDispatcherContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Exception handler wrapper that forwards to main exception handler implementation\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EAX register to local stack variable\n2. Clear DF (direction flag) for string operations\n3. Build parameter stack frame with additional runtime context\n4. Call FUN_6fb9b884 with exception record, context, flags, and internal registers\n5. Clean up stack (8 parameters, 3 pushes = 0x20 bytes)\n6. Move return value to output parameter\n7. Restore registers and return\n\nParameters:\nPEXCEPTION_RECORD pExceptionRecord - Exception information record\nPVOID pContext - Context record pointer\nDWORD dwExceptionFlags - Exception handling flags (0=first, 1=nested)\ndword dwDispatcherContext - Dispatcher context (implicit in in_EAX register)\n\nReturns:\ndword - Exception disposition (EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_EXECUTION, EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH, etc)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Saves EAX immediately at function entry (implicit register parameter)\n- Uses DF flag clear for subsequent operations\n- Passes implicit register value via stack to FUN_6fb9b884",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
