      "name": "FormatStringToBufferV",
      "signature": "int FormatStringToBufferV(char * szDst, byte * pbFormat, uint * pVarArgs)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Formats a string using printf-style specifiers into a destination buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize position pointer (szPos) and guard counter (nGuard=0x7FFFFFFF)\n2. Set mode flag (dwMode=0x42='B') for buffer output\n3. Call internal format parser (FUN_6fdd8155) with format string and varargs\n4. Decrement guard counter\n5. If overflow detected (nGuard < 0), call error handler (FUN_6fdd71a6)\n6. Otherwise null-terminate the output string\n\nParameters:\n- szDst (char*): Destination buffer for formatted output\n- pbFormat (byte*): Printf-style format string\n- pVarArgs (uint*): Pointer to variadic argument list\n\nReturns:\n- int: Number of characters written (from format parser)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x42 (66): Buffer output mode flag ('B')\n- 0x7FFFFFFF: Maximum integer guard for overflow detection\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fdd8155: Core printf format string parser\n- FUN_6fdd71a6: Stream error/flush handler",
