      "name": "HandleStructuredException",
      "signature": "void HandleStructuredException(PEXCEPTION_RECORD pExcRecord, PVOID pBasePtr, DWORD dwContext, uint dwUnknown, int nFrameCount, byte * pbFrameData, byte * pbRestoreData, int * pnState, int nStateIndex, PVOID pUnwindContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Handles structured exception by unwinding and restoring execution context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If restore data provided, copy from frame data to restore buffer\n2. If unwind context is null, use base pointer\n3. Call exception unwinder with context and record\n4. Process frame state with frame count and current state\n5. Increment state counter at base offset 8\n6. Create SEH context from exception record and parameters\n7. If SEH context valid, restore and jump to handler\n\nParameters:\npExcRecord - Windows exception record structure\npBasePtr - Base address of exception context\ndwContext - Exception context flags\ndwUnknown - Unknown context parameter\nnFrameCount - Number of frames in exception stack\npbFrameData - Pointer to frame data buffer\npbRestoreData - Pointer to restoration buffer (null = skip)\npnState - Pointer to current state value [read/write]\nnStateIndex - Current state index in stack\npUnwindContext - Custom unwind context (null = use pBasePtr)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - function always returns (no return value)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:62a2e5dc1ebafcfcaf171ff66287ccbb588b91d082383c96cdbea2d2e1c48eca",
