      "name": "ValidateExceptionHandlerStructure",
      "signature": "int ValidateExceptionHandlerStructure(int * pExceptionRecord)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates and initializes an exception handler structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dereference pExceptionRecord to get handler structure pointer\n2. Check if structure has magic marker 0xe06d7363 at offset 0x0\n3. Check if field at offset 0x10 equals 3\n4. Check if field at offset 0x14 equals 0x19930520 (May 2001 timestamp)\n5. If all three conditions match: call SetupStructuredExceptionHandler() and return its result\n6. Otherwise, check if g_pfnExceptionHandler function pointer is set (non-NULL)\n7. If set, validate handler with FUN_6fba1500()\n8. If validation succeeds, invoke handler function pointer with pExceptionRecord parameter\n9. Return handler result; if no handler, return 0 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pExceptionRecord (int *): Pointer to exception handler structure\n\nReturns:\n- Handler function result (typically 0 for success or error code)\n- 0 if no handler is configured\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number validation (0xe06d7363) identifies known handler structure\n- Handler is optional - returns 0 if no g_pfnExceptionHandler set\n- FUN_6fba1500 must validate handler before invocation",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
