      "name": "CRT_AllocateStreamBuffer",
      "signature": "int * CRT_AllocateStreamBuffer(int * pFileStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int *",
      "comment": "CRT_AllocateStreamBuffer - Allocates or assigns an I/O buffer for a FILE stream structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment global stream buffer allocation counter (g_dwStreamBufferAllocCount)\n2. Attempt to allocate 0x1000 (4096) byte buffer via _malloc\n3. Store allocation result in stream structure at offset +0x8 (buffer pointer field)\n4. If allocation succeeded:\n   a. Set flag 0x8 in stream flags at offset +0xC (big buffer allocated)\n   b. Set buffer size to 0x1000 at offset +0x18\n5. If allocation failed (NULL returned):\n   a. Set flag 0x4 in stream flags at offset +0xC (using internal buffer)\n   b. Point buffer to internal 2-byte buffer at stream offset +0x14\n   c. Set buffer size to 2 at offset +0x18\n6. Clear bytes-in-buffer count at offset +0x4\n7. Set current buffer pointer at offset +0x0 to buffer base\n8. Return buffer pointer\n\nParameters:\n  pFileStream (int *) - Pointer to FILE stream structure\n\nReturns:\n  int * - Pointer to allocated/assigned buffer (offset +0x8 of stream)\n\nFILE Stream Structure Layout (relevant fields):\n  Offset  Size  Field               Description\n  +0x00   4     pCurrentPos         Current position in buffer\n  +0x04   4     nBytesInBuffer      Count of bytes remaining in buffer\n  +0x08   4     pBufferBase         Base pointer of I/O buffer\n  +0x0C   4     dwFlags             Stream flags (0x4=internal buf, 0x8=allocated buf)\n  +0x14   2     abInternalBuffer    Internal 2-byte fallback buffer\n  +0x18   4     dwBufferSize        Size of buffer in bytes\n\nFlag Bits (offset +0x0C):\n  0x04 - Using internal 2-byte buffer (allocation failed)\n  0x08 - Using dynamically allocated 4KB buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - On malloc failure, stream uses tiny 2-byte internal buffer for minimal I/O\n  - This is a CRT internal function called during stream initialization",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
