      "name": "BinarySearchLocaleEntry",
      "signature": "undefined BinarySearchLocaleEntry(void * this, int param_1, int param_2, byte * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Performs binary search on a locale entry array to find a matching locale by name.\n\nSearches the sorted locale array for an entry whose name matches the search key\nusing case-insensitive comparison. When a match is found, stores a pointer to\nthe locale code string in the output parameter.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize low bound to 0 and continue flag to true\n2. Return immediately if array is empty (nHighIndex < 0)\n3. Loop while low <= high and continue flag is set:\n   a. Calculate midpoint: nMidIndex = (nLowIndex + nHighIndex) / 2\n   b. Get locale name pointer from pLocaleArray[nMidIndex].szLocaleName (offset 0)\n   c. Compare search key with locale name (case-insensitive)\n   d. If match (result == 0):\n      - Store pointer to locale code (offset +4) in *lpszSearchKey\n      - Clear continue flag to exit loop\n   e. If search key < entry (result < 0): narrow to lower half (nHighIndex = mid - 1)\n   f. If search key > entry (result > 0): narrow to upper half (nLowIndex = mid + 1)\n4. Return (result stored via output parameter)\n\nParameters:\n- this (ECX, IMPLICIT): Context pointer passed to CompareStringsIgnoreCase (auto-parameter)\n- nLocaleArrayPtr: Base address of LocaleEntry array (8 bytes each: char* szName, char* szCode)\n- nHighIndex: Upper bound index for binary search (array_size - 1)\n- lpszSearchKey: IN/OUT - Input: pointer to search key string; Output: pointer to locale code if found\n\nReturns:\n- void (result communicated via lpszSearchKey output parameter)\n- On match: *lpszSearchKey points to szLocaleCode string in matched entry\n- On no match: *lpszSearchKey unchanged\n\nStructure Layout (LocaleEntry - 8 bytes):\n  Offset | Size | Field        | Type   | Description\n  -------|------|--------------|--------|-------------------------\n  0x00   | 4    | szLocaleName | char*  | Locale display name\n  0x04   | 4    | szLocaleCode | char*  | Locale identifier code\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty array (nHighIndex < 0): Returns immediately without modification\n- No match found: Loop exits normally, *lpszSearchKey unchanged",
