      "name": "CountAlphabeticCharacters",
      "signature": "int CountAlphabeticCharacters(char * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Counts consecutive alphabetic characters at the beginning of a string\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize EAX (nCharCount) to 0\n  2. Loop: Load next byte from string\n  3. Increment string pointer (EDX)\n  4. Check if character is uppercase A-Z (0x41-0x5A)\n  5. If yes, increment counter and continue loop\n  6. Check if character is lowercase a-z (0x61-0x7A)\n  7. If yes, increment counter and continue loop\n  8. If neither uppercase nor lowercase, exit loop\n  9. Return character count in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  szString - Pointer to null-terminated string (char*)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX - Number of consecutive alphabetic characters at start\n  \nSpecial Cases:\n  Empty string or non-alphabetic first character returns 0\n  Stops counting at first non-letter (including null terminator)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
