      "name": "ProcessDateFormatSpecifier",
      "signature": "undefined ProcessDateFormatSpecifier(char param_1, int * param_2, byte * param_3, uint * param_4, int param_5)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Format and output a single date/time format specifier to output buffer.\\n\\n  Algorithm:\\n  1. Decode format character chSpec to determine output format\\n  2. Extract corresponding date/time value from pDateTime array\\n  3. Set global separator state (g_dwLastCharSeparator to g_dwCurrentCharSeparator)\\n  4. Call numeric formatter (FUN_0040a6ad) or string formatter (FUN_0040a686)\\n  5. Return with buffer/size pointers updated\\n\\n  Parameters:\\n    chSpec: Single format character ('%', 'A'-'Z', 'a'-'z')\\n    pDateTime: Pointer to 9-element array [second,minute,hour,day,month,year,weekday,YDay,Y2k]\\n    pbBuffer: Pointer to output buffer (double-indirect: *pbBuffer is write pointer)\\n    pcbRemaining: Pointer to remaining buffer size in bytes (decremented on write)\\n    nContext: Base address of context structure containing string tables\\n              Offsets: 0x00=weekday_abbr[], 0x04=month_abbr[], 0x68/0x1c=month_full[]\\n                       0x38/0xa0/0xa4/0xa8=separator tables, 0x98/0x9c=am/pm strings\\n\\n  Returns:\\n  void - modifies output buffer and remaining size via pointers\\n\\n  Special Cases:\\n  - '%': Outputs literal '%' character\\n  - 'I'/'m': Month as 1-12 (handles 12-hour to month offset)\\n  - 'Y'/'y': Year with offset calculations for century\\n  - 'W'/'U': Week number with special divisor logic (0x7 or 0xc)\\n  - 'c'/'x': Uses separator state (g_dwLastCharSeparator) to switch tables\\n  - 'Z'/'p': Conditional string selection based on hour value >= 0xb (noon check)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:0916c5917506fd5ea8571a47d499a7419e8ed467c1a0ff52018c8fe2ae6237da",
