      "name": "IntToStringEx",
      "signature": "char * IntToStringEx(uint param_1, char * param_2, uint param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Converts an integer to string representation with radix support\n  \n  Algorithm:\n  1. Check if radix is 10 (decimal) and value is negative (signed int)\n  2. Set negative flag if both conditions are true\n  3. Call ConvertIntToString with all parameters and negative flag\n  4. Return pointer to output string buffer\n  \n  Parameters:\n  - nValue: Integer value to convert (may be negative for radix 10)\n  - pszBuffer: Pointer to output string buffer\n  - dwRadix: Numeric base (2-36), typically 10 for decimal\n  \n  Returns:\n  - pszBuffer: Pointer to the formatted string output\n  \n  Special Cases:\n  - Only handles negative values for decimal (base 10) conversion\n  - Other bases treat input as unsigned",
