      "name": "InitializeHardwareCelData",
      "signature": "void InitializeHardwareCelData(byte * pCelData, int * pCelContext, int * pGfxNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initialize hardware-accelerated CEL sprite data structures for rendering.\n\nThis function sets up hardware CEL frame data by allocating pool memory for\nthe graphics block, verifying async load completion, and iterating through\nframe data to populate hardware rendering offsets.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pCelContext is not NULL (assert if NULL)\n2. Validate pGfxNode is not NULL (assert if NULL)\n3. Check pCelData bit 0 (INDEXED flag) - assert if set (hardware mode requires non-indexed)\n4. Check pGfxNode[0x28] (hardware handle) - assert if already initialized\n5. Calculate total frames: bWidth * bHeight (from GfxNode offsets 0x24 and 0x21)\n6. Allocate pool memory: size = (frames * 11) * 4 bytes using AllocPoolMemoryTracked\n7. Zero-fill allocated memory using STOSD/STOSB\n8. Call GetAsyncResult to verify async file operation completed\n9. Assert async result is valid\n10. Calculate frame data: bWidth * bHeight product for iteration\n11. Loop through each frame:\n    a. Read frame header from pCelData offset table\n    b. Validate frame size <= 0x100\n    c. Calculate frame offset and store in hardware block\n    d. Advance frame pointer by size + 0x23 header\n12. Set pGfxNode[0x28] = 1 to mark hardware data initialized\n13. Return (void)\n\nParameters:\n  pCelData (byte *, ECX) - Pointer to CEL file data containing frame offset table\n  pCelContext (int *, EDX) - Pointer to CEL context structure with sprite metadata\n  pGfxNode (int *, stack) - Pointer to graphics node structure to initialize\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, modifies pGfxNode in place\n\nError Handling:\n  - NULL pCelContext: Triggers FogAssert at line 0x439\n  - NULL pGfxNode: Triggers FogAssert at line 0x43A\n  - INDEXED flag set: Triggers FogAssert at line 0x43B\n  - Already initialized: Triggers FogAssert at line 0x43E\n  - Async result NULL: Triggers FogAssert at line 0x450\n  - Invalid frame size: Triggers FogFatalError with formatted path\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x24 - Offset in GfxNode for bWidth (frame width)\n  0x21 - Offset in GfxNode for bHeight (frame height)\n  0x22 - Offset in GfxNode for direction index\n  0x28 - Offset in GfxNode for hardware initialization flag\n  0x2c - Offset in pCelData for frame offset table base\n  0xb0 - Offset in GfxNode for async data pointer\n  0x100 - Maximum valid frame size (256 bytes)\n  0x23 - Frame header size added during iteration\n\nRelated Functions:\n  AllocPoolMemoryTracked - Allocates tracked pool memory from heap\n  GetAsyncResult - Retrieves result from async file operation\n  FogAssert - Debug assertion handler\n  ReportError - Fatal error reporting with termination\n  CreateUnitFilePath - Generates file path for error messages\n  FormatStringVarArgs - Formats error message strings",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:0a351a38f26512c85d1ac6fa36fff73e",
