      "name": "InitializeSpriteFrameData",
      "signature": "dword InitializeSpriteFrameData(int * pCelContext, byte * pCelData, int nFrames, int nDirections)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize sprite frame data with frame offsets and async decompression handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate GfxNode structure (184 bytes) from sprite cache heap\n2. Clear all 46 dword fields in GfxNode to zero via REP STOSD\n3. Copy frame IDs from CelContext fields 0x30-0x40 to GfxNode 0x0C-0x1C\n4. Determine frame offset range based on CelData type (1=Standard, 2=Static, 3=Directional, 4=Simple, 6=Rotation)\n5. Calculate start and end frame offsets from CelData offset table at +0x1C\n6. Populate GfxBlock direction offsets array (nOffsets[32]) with relative offsets\n7. Register async decompression handler via InitAsyncFileOperation for sprite data\n8. Create palette cache hash entry via AllocateAndLinkResourceNode linking CelContext to GfxNode\n9. For non-INDEXED type, call InitializeHardwareCelData and CalculateSpriteFrameOffset\n10. Return 1 if successful, 0 if INDEXED format or already initialized\n\nParameters:\npCelContext (int *) - CelContext structure containing frame metadata and palette info\npCelData (byte *) - CelData structure with frame offset table and compressed sprite data\nnFrames (int) - Number of frames to initialize (usually 1)\nnDirections (int) - Number of directions per frame (1-8)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Successfully initialized sprite frame data\n0 - Frame data already initialized or INDEXED type requiring separate CEL decompression\n\nStructure Layout - GfxNode (0xB8 = 184 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field            Description\n0x00    4     reserved         Reserved\n0x04    4     field_1          CelContext[0x28] - palette info\n0x08    4     field_2          CelContext[0x24] - resource ID\n0x0C    4     field_3          CelContext[0x30] - frame ID base\n0x10    4     field_4          CelContext[0x34] - frame ID ext1\n0x14    4     field_5          CelContext[0x38] - frame ID ext2\n0x18    4     field_6          CelContext[0x3C] - frame ID ext3\n0x1C    4     field_7          CelContext[0x40] - frame ID ext4\n0x20    1     flags            Bit 0=INDEXED, Bit 2=async pending\n0x21    1     nDirections      Direction count\n0x22    1     nTotalFrames     Total frames (nFrames * nDirections)\n0x23    1     nRotations       Rotation count (pCelData[0x14] + 1)\n0x24    1     directionByte    Direction byte (pCelData[0x18])\n0x2C    128   nOffsets[32]     Direction frame offsets array\n0xB0    4     lpAsyncData      Async operation handle\n0xB4    4     pCacheItem       Back-pointer to cache item\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xB8 (184) - GfxNode structure size\n0x2E (46)  - Loop count to clear 46 dwords\n0x1C       - Offset table start in CelData\n0x20 (32)  - MAX_DIROFFSETS array size limit\n0x04       - Async pending flag in GfxNode.flags\n0x01       - INDEXED format flag in pCelData[0]\n0x02       - Alpha/transparency flag in pCelData[0]\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert on null pCacheItem allocation (line 0x4E8)\n- FogAssert on null pCelData, pGfxNode, pCelContext (lines 0x268-0x26A)\n- FogAssert if nDirections != 1 for rotation types (line 0x272)\n- FogAssert if frame data size is zero (line 0x29C)\n- FogAssert if lpAsyncData already set (line 0x29E)\n- FogAssert if direction index exceeds MAX_DIROFFSETS (line 0x2AF)\n- FogAssert if negative offset calculated (line 0x2B1)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
