      "name": "InitializeSpriteGraphicsBlock",
      "signature": "dword InitializeSpriteGraphicsBlock(int nCelContext, byte * ptCelData, int nFrameWidth, int nFrameHeight)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes a sprite graphics block for CEL animation rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0xB8-byte graphics block from cache manager\n2. Zero-initialize 46 dwords (0x2E * 4 = 0xB8 bytes) via REP STOSD\n3. Copy animation context fields from nCelContext structure:\n   - Frame dimensions at offsets 0x30-0x40 to block offsets 0x0C-0x1C\n4. Validate input pointers (ptCelData, block, context) with assertions\n5. Calculate frame offsets based on width*height for multi-frame sprites\n6. Compute offset table differences for frame boundary detection\n7. Set up async file loader parameters if flag 0x02 set on ptCelData\n8. Call InitAsyncFileOperation to queue graphics loading\n9. Link allocated block into graphics cache hash table\n10. Set status flags: 0x01 for deferred, 0x02 for immediate load\n\nParameters:\n  nCelContext (ECX) - Pointer to CEL animation context structure containing\n                      frame dimensions and animation parameters\n  ptCelData (EDX) - Pointer to CEL data header with flags byte at offset 0\n                    Flag 0x01: Deferred loading mode\n                    Flag 0x02: Async file operation mode\n  nFrameWidth (Stack+0x4) - Width of sprite frame in pixels\n  nFrameHeight (Stack+0x8) - Height of sprite frame in pixels\n\nReturns:\n  1 (EAX) - Success, graphics block initialized and linked\n  0 (EAX) - Failure, allocation failed or async operation failed\n\nError Handling:\n  Line 0x2F2 - Null ptCelData assertion failure\n  Line 0x2F3 - Null graphics node assertion failure\n  Line 0x2F4 - Null context pointer assertion failure\n  Line 0x30C - Zero offset difference assertion\n  Line 0x30D - Block already has loader attached\n  Line 0x321 - Frame index exceeds 0x21 limit\n  Line 0x323 - Negative offset difference\n  Line 0x338 - Async loader setup line marker\n  Line 0x343 - Sync loader setup line marker\n  Line 0x561 - Hash table link failure\n\nStructure Layout (Graphics Block at ESI):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Description\n  0x00    4     pBlockData    Pointer to allocated block data\n  0x04    4     dwDataSize    Size of CEL data buffer\n  0x08    4     dwFileHandle  File handle for async operations\n  0x0C    4     dwFrameOff1   First frame offset from context+0x30\n  0x10    4     dwFrameOff2   Second frame offset from context+0x34\n  0x14    4     dwFrameOff3   Third frame offset from context+0x38\n  0x18    4     dwFrameOff4   Fourth frame offset from context+0x3C\n  0x1C    4     dwFrameOff5   Fifth frame offset from context+0x40\n  0x20    1     bStatusFlags  Status: 0x01=deferred, 0x02=immediate, 0x04=async\n  0x21    1     bFrameHeight  Calculated frame height\n  0x22    1     bFrameArea    Width * Height product (low byte)\n  0x23    1     bDirCount     Direction count + 1\n  0x24    1     bFrameIdx     Current frame index\n  0x2C    N*4   adwOffsets    Frame offset table (variable size)\n  0xB0    4     pAsyncLoader  Async file operation handle\n  0xB4    4     pCacheLink    Back-link to cache block node\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xB8 - Graphics block allocation size (184 bytes)\n  0x2E - Number of dwords to zero (46)\n  0x21 - Maximum frame index limit (33 frames)\n  0x6FF02BC0 - Global graphics cache manager pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:43a9eec5c7ccd4941e8fd0522a8aaa17",
