      "name": "BuildTileDisplayGraphics",
      "signature": "void BuildTileDisplayGraphics(uint * pTile, int nBaseOffset)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Builds tile display graphics by iterating coordinate list, allocating square buffers, and filling with pixel data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pTile and nBaseOffset (assert failures terminate)\n2. For each coordinate in g_pawTileCoordinateList:\n   a. Allocate 0x600-byte square buffer via AllocClientMemory\n   b. Zero-fill buffer (0x180 dwords)\n   c. Extract 3-byte RGB from pTile[0xd], fill 0x200 pixels\n   d. Copy pixel data from source (15 rows with variable width)\n   e. Verify pixels match expected color; flag errors with 0x2001\n   f. Register square via UpdatePaletteIndex or link error component\n3. Reset pTile viewport: [0]=0, [1]=0, [2]=0xa0, [3]=0xffffff80\n\nParameters:\n- pTile (uint*): Tile structure with image data at [0xd], component list at [0x16]\n- nBaseOffset (int): Base offset for source tile image buffer\n\nReturns:\n- void: Modifies pTile in-place\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x600: Square buffer size (0x180 dwords = 0x200 3-byte pixels)\n- 0x153, 0x1a6: Memory allocator codes\n- 0x185: Palette registration code\n- 0x2001: Error flag for pixel mismatch",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:3bd72a4d865e05d8333374f74fa25c19",
