      "name": "AssignTileToFirstEmptySlot",
      "signature": "void AssignTileToFirstEmptySlot(int * pnIndices, byte * pszName)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Assigns a tile name to the first empty slot in the tile library projection array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert pnIndices and pszName are not NULL\n2. Loop through indices array (up to 32 entries)\n   - Find first slot where index value equals 0\n   - Call LoadOrCreateTileHash to assign the name\n   - Return immediately after assignment\n3. If all 32 indices are non-zero, assert failure\n\nParameters:\n- pnIndices (int*): Pointer to tile projection index array (max 32 entries)\n- pszName (byte*): Tile name string to assign to first available slot\n\nReturns:\n- void: Terminates on assertion failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Maximum tile projects allowed (MAX_TILEPROJECT)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:d599231ae5c788c503189246ef3b4371",
