      "name": "AdjustFileBufferBounds",
      "signature": "int AdjustFileBufferBounds(BufferManager * pBufferManager, FileBuffer * pFileBuffer, byte * pbData, uint dwNewSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Adjusts the size of a memory buffer within a constrained allocation pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load current buffer size from pBuffer[0]\n  2. Calculate pool entry address: pMemPool[0x18 + ((pBuffer - pMemPool[0x10]) >> 0xc) * 8]\n  3. Compare newSize against currentSize:\n     - If newSize < currentSize: shrink operation, return freed bytes to pool with marker 0xf1\n     - If newSize == currentSize: no change required, return success\n     - If newSize > currentSize: expand operation, validate zero-padding from currentSize to newSize\n  4. For expansion, validate buffer space constraints:\n     - Check newSize does not exceed pool boundary (pMemPool + 0xf8)\n     - Scan all bytes from currentSize to newSize, all must be zero\n  5. Update buffer size field to newSize\n  6. If payload pointer at pSize[0] falls within buffer range, adjust pointer to newSize\n  7. Count zero bytes following payload (stored in pSize[1]) for size tracking\n  8. Update pool free space accounting at pMemPool[0x18]\n  9. Return success (1) or failure (0) on validation errors\n\nParameters:\n  pMemPool: Pointer to memory pool structure, contains offsets 0x10 (base), 0x18 (free space)\n  pSize: Pointer to size tracking structure (2 DWORDs): [0] = payload pointer, [1] = size\n  pBuffer: Byte pointer to buffer being resized, pBuffer[0] contains current size\n  dwNewSize: New size in bytes (0x0 to 0xf8 bytes relative to buffer start)\n\nReturns:\n  1 (success) if resize operation completed with all validations passing\n  0 (failure) if any validation failed: boundary exceeded, padding not all-zeros, pointer adjustment failed\n  On failure: buffer size and pool state remain unchanged\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Expansion requires entire padding region to be zero-filled (detects overlapping allocations)\n  - Payload pointer within buffer triggers pointer and size recalculation\n  - Pool boundary check prevents buffer overflow (max size = 0xf8 bytes)\n  - Shrink returns freed bytes to pool accounting immediately\n  - Marker 0xf1 written to indicate pool entry was modified",
