      "name": "CloneTileProject",
      "signature": "void CloneTileProject(dword * pSrcProject, dword * * ppDstProject, void * pPalette)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Creates a deep copy of a tile project structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate source project pointer and TILEPROJECT_FLAGS flag\n2. Allocate 0x114 bytes for new project structure (0x45 dwords)\n3. Zero-initialize then memcpy source project data\n4. Clear TILEPROJECT_FLAGS bit, allocate tile array (nTiles * 0x60 bytes)\n5. For each tile: copy 0x60 bytes (0x18 dwords) of tile data\n6. Allocate component array (nComps * 0x14 bytes) per tile\n7. For each component: compress palette data or clear if empty\n8. Store cloned project pointer to output parameter\n\nParameters:\n- pSrcProject (dword*): Source tile project structure\n- ppDstProject (dword**): Output pointer to receive cloned project\n- pPalette (void*): Palette data for compression operations\n\nReturns:\n- void (output via ppDstProject)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x114 (276): TileProject struct size in bytes\n- 0x45 (69): TileProject struct size in dwords\n- 0x60 (96): TileData struct stride\n- 0x18 (24): TileData struct size in dwords\n- 0x14 (20): TileComponent struct stride\n- 0x1000: TILECOMP_GAMES flag for chunk encoding\n- 0x2000: TILECOMP_GRID flag for grid processing",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04c",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:54485a39d5e08aa549fb65be7ebc5b05",
