      "name": "GetGraphicsConfig",
      "signature": "undefined4 GetGraphicsConfig(uint param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "GetRotationTableEntry - Validate parameters and return entry from rotation lookup table\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate dwRotationLevel <= 0x3f (63 max rotation levels)\n2. Call GetFirstBit(dwValue) to get bit position (must be 0-7)\n3. Compute popcount of dwValue using bit manipulation (shifts and masks)\n4. Validate popcount == 1 (exactly one bit set)\n5. If all validations pass, calculate table index = GetFirstBit(dwValue) * 64 + dwRotationLevel\n6. Return value from rotation table at [g_adLevelRotationTable + index*4]\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporaries optimized away (iVar1, uVar2 in SSA form).\n\nParameters:\n  dwRotationLevel (uint): Rotation level index, must be 0-63 (0x00-0x3f)\n  dwValue (uint): Bit pattern, must have exactly one bit set (0x01, 0x02, 0x04, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Entry from rotation lookup table at calculated index\n  On validation failure: Calls Ordinal_10023 (error handler) with error code and exits\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Invalid rotation level (>0x3f) triggers assertion at line 0x1da\n  - Invalid bit count (!=1 bit set) triggers assertion at line 0x1dc\n  - dwValue with multiple bits set triggers assertion at line 0x1db\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x3f (63): Maximum rotation level index\n  0x8: Maximum bit position from GetFirstBit\n  0x40 (64): Stride between rotation level tables (64 entries per level)\n  0x77777777, 0x33333333, 0x11111111: Popcount bit masks\n  0x0f0f0f0f: Final mask for popcount\n  0xff (255): Modulo for popcount verification\n  0x1da, 0x1db, 0x1dc: Assertion line numbers\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6fe20aa0 (GetFirstBit) - Returns bit position (0-7) for single-bit values\n- Ordinal_10023 (AssertionFailed/ErrorHandler) - Fog.dll error reporting function",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
