      "name": "AllocateCelFrameBuffer",
      "signature": "undefined4 AllocateCelFrameBuffer(int param_1, undefined4 param_2, undefined4 param_3, undefined4 param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Allocates a frame buffer for a cel file and invokes a callback handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate cel file has 24-bit flag set (dwFlags & 0x4)\n2. If flag missing, assert with FogAssertFail and terminate process\n3. Calculate buffer size: width * height * 4 + 0x18 header bytes\n4. Allocate frame buffer via AllocClientMemory\n5. Initialize buffer: magic=6, flags (masked 0xF8), width, height, accumulator=0\n6. Look up callback function from g_pFrameBufferCallbacks[pCelFile->nTopOffset]\n7. Invoke callback with dwCallbackParam1 and dwCallbackParam2\n8. Store allocated buffer pointer to output parameter\n9. Return true for success\n\nParameters:\n- pCelFile (CelFile*): Cel file structure, must have CELFILE_24BIT flag (0x4)\n- dwCallbackIndex (uint): Unused - callback index comes from pCelFile->nTopOffset\n- dwCallbackParam1 (uint): First parameter passed to callback function\n- dwCallbackParam2 (uint): Second parameter passed to callback function\n\nReturns:\n- true: Always returns true on success (terminates on failure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4: CELFILE_24BIT flag in dwFlags\n- 0x6: Frame buffer magic signature\n- 0xF8: Mask to preserve upper 5 bits of flags\n- 0x18 (24): Frame buffer header size in bytes\n- 0x29B (667): Source line number for assertion\n- 0x29F (671): Source line number for allocation\n\nRelated Functions:\n- AllocClientMemory: Allocates memory from heap\n- FogAssertFail: Logs assertion failure\n- TerminateProcessWithCode: Exits process with code",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "NOP",
