      "name": "ConvertCelFileTo8BitPalette",
      "signature": "undefined ConvertCelFileTo8BitPalette(int param_1, int param_2, undefined * param_3, undefined4 param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Converts a 24-bit RGB CEL file to an 8-bit palettized format using a color lookup callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate source CEL has CELFILE_24BIT flag (0x4) set, assert if not\n2. Calculate total frame count as nWidth * nHeight from CEL header\n3. For each frame in the source CEL:\n   a. Allocate temporary buffer for palettized pixel data (frame.w * frame.h bytes)\n   b. For each pixel in frame (3 bytes RGB per source pixel):\n      - If pixel matches dwTransparentColor (R,G,B), write 0x00 (transparent index)\n      - Otherwise call pfnColorLookup(R, G, B) to get palette index\n      - Assert if lookup returns 0 (invalid palette match)\n   c. Compress palettized data using CompressItemDataLine\n   d. Allocate new frame structure with compressed data\n   e. Copy frame header fields (type, width, height, etc.)\n   f. Copy compressed data to new frame\n   g. Release temporary buffer\n   h. Store new frame pointer in destination CEL frame array\n4. Function returns after all frames are converted\n\nParameters:\n  nSrcCel (ECX) - Pointer to source 24-bit CEL file structure\n  nDestCel (EDX) - Pointer to destination 8-bit CEL file structure  \n  pfnColorLookup - Callback function: byte pfnColorLookup(byte R, byte G, byte B)\n                   Returns palette index for given RGB color, 0 indicates failure\n  dwTransparentColor - RGB color value to treat as transparent (index 0)\n                       Format: 0x00BBGGRR (low byte = R, next = G, high word low byte = B)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value. Destination CEL is populated with converted frames.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if source CEL lacks CELFILE_24BIT flag\n  - Asserts if color lookup returns 0 for non-transparent pixel\n\nCalled By:\n  Address 0x6fe2a1bc",
