      "name": "FilterCppException",
      "signature": "int FilterCppException(_EXCEPTION_POINTERS * pExceptionPointers)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Filter function for C++ exception handling\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve exception record from exception pointers structure\n2. Check if exception code matches Microsoft C++ exception magic (0xE06D7363)\n3. If not a C++ exception, return 0 (EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH)\n4. If C++ exception detected, tail-call to SetupStructuredExceptionHandler\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionPointers (_EXCEPTION_POINTERS *) - Pointer to exception information structure\n    containing ExceptionRecord and ContextRecord for current exception\n\nReturns:\n  int - Exception filter result:\n    0 (EXCEPTION_CONTINUE_SEARCH) - Not a C++ exception, continue handler search\n    Tail-call result from SetupStructuredExceptionHandler if C++ exception\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xE06D7363 - Microsoft Visual C++ exception code ('msc' | 0xE0000000)\n               This identifies exceptions thrown via C++ throw keyword\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses tail-call optimization (JMP instead of CALL+RET) to SetupStructuredExceptionHandler\n  - The extraout_EAX in decompilation represents return value from tail-called function",
