      "name": "CountValidLockContextEntities",
      "signature": "int CountValidLockContextEntities(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Wrapper that counts all valid lock context entities in count mode\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ProcessLockContextEntities with mode 1 (Count Mode)\n2. Return count of successfully validated entities\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint: Count of successfully validated lock context entities (>= 0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if no lock context entries exist\n- NULL entries and entities without active flags are skipped\n- Validation failures are ignored in count mode\n\nNotes:\n- This is a thin wrapper around ProcessLockContextEntities(1)\n- Uses __stdcall but internally calls __cdecl callee, stack cleaned via POP ECX",
