      "name": "GameDataCollectionDestructor",
      "signature": "void * GameDataCollectionDestructor(void * this, void * pThis, byte fDeleteContents)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Destructor for GameDataCollection objects with optional memory deallocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Call DestroyGameDataCollection to clean up internal data structures\n2. Check if deletion flag (bDeleteFlag & 0x1) is set  \n3. If deletion flag is set and object pointer is not null:\n   - Call Ordinal_403 (operator delete) with object pointer\n   - Pass delete parameters: s_delete_6fbae0d8, 0xffffffff, 0\n4. Return original object pointer for chaining\n\nParameters:\n\n- this (GameDataCollection *): Pointer to GameDataCollection object to destroy\n- bDeleteFlag (byte): Deletion control flags, bit 0 controls memory deallocation\n\nReturns:\n\n- void *: Returns the original object pointer (this) for destructor chaining\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If bDeleteFlag & 0x1 == 0: Object destructor called but memory not freed\n- If this == NULL: DestroyGameDataCollection still called, no memory deallocation\n- s_delete_6fbae0d8: String literal \"delete\" passed to operator delete for debugging\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x1: Deletion flag mask - bit 0 controls memory deallocation\n- 0xffffffff: Size parameter passed to operator delete (-1, unknown size)  \n- 0: Additional parameter passed to operator delete (unused flags)\n\nError Handling:\n- No explicit error checking - relies on called functions for validation\n- NULL pointer check only performed before memory deallocation\n- Operator delete handles invalid pointers internally",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b1e56c9ff95470fd732bf8bc61a9f5d9743b18b0442071ed91610cd9e6bea4fe",
