      "name": "ResizeNodeContainer",
      "signature": "void ResizeNodeContainer(void * this, NodeContainer * pContainer, dword dwNewCapacity)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Resize a NodeContainer to accommodate a new capacity.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if requested capacity <= current capacity (shrink path)\n2. Early exit if requested capacity <= current size (no growth needed)\n3. Calculate growth factor: power-of-2 alignment for small sizes, linear (0x15) for large\n4. Align new capacity to growth factor boundary\n5. Initialize new elements from current capacity to aligned capacity\n6. Attempt SMemReAlloc on existing buffer; if fails, allocate fresh via SMemAlloc\n7. If fresh allocation with existing data, copy old nodes via UnlinkListNodes loop\n8. Free old buffer via SMemFree after copy\n9. Initialize any additional elements beyond aligned capacity\n10. Update container's capacity and size fields\n\nParameters:\npContainer (ECX, NodeContainer*): Pointer to the container being resized\n  Offset 0x00: dwCount - Current size/count\n  Offset 0x04: dwCapacity - Current capacity\n  Offset 0x08: pNodes - Node array pointer (12 bytes per node)\n  Offset 0x0C: dwGrowthFactor - Growth factor (0 = auto, 0x15 = linear mode)\ndwNewCapacity (Stack+4): Requested new capacity\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies container in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If dwNewCapacity <= capacity: Shrinks by calling UnlinkListNodes on excess nodes\n- If dwNewCapacity <= size: Updates capacity field only, no reallocation\n- If growth factor is 0: Uses power-of-2 alignment for sizes < 21\n- If growth factor is 0 and size >= 21: Sets linear growth mode (0x15)\n\nMemory Operations:\n- SMemReAlloc (Storm.Ordinal_405): Attempts in-place reallocation\n- SMemAlloc (Storm.Ordinal_403): Fallback fresh allocation\n- SMemFree (Storm.Ordinal_401): Frees old buffer after copy\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x15 (21): Threshold for switching to linear growth mode\n0x0C (12): Stride size for nodes\n0x10: SMemReAlloc flags parameter",
