      "name": "CloseAndCleanupStreamStructures",
      "signature": "int CloseAndCleanupStreamStructures(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes all closeable stream structures and deallocates dynamic entries.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section 2 for thread-safe access to stream table\n2. Iterate through stream structure table starting at index 3\n3. For each valid stream structure:\n   a. Check if flags byte has closeable bits set (0x83 mask)\n   b. If closeable, call ThreadSafeFileClose and increment closed count\n   c. For dynamic entries (index >= 20), also:\n      - Delete the embedded critical section at offset 0x20\n      - Deallocate the stream structure memory\n      - Clear the table pointer entry\n4. Release critical section 2\n5. Return count of successfully closed streams\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of stream files successfully closed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  3     - First stream index to process (indices 0-2 are reserved)\n  0x13  - Last static stream index (0x14+ are dynamic)\n  0x83  - Closeable stream flags mask\n  0x20  - Offset of embedded CRITICAL_SECTION in stream structure\n  2     - Critical section index for stream table access",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
