      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Establishes Windows SEH exception handler frame for unwinding exception context.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current TIB (Thread Information Block) exception chain head from FS:[0x0]\n2. Push exception handler marker (-0x1) onto stack\n3. Push address of exception handler routine (LAB_6fc320aa) onto stack\n4. Push saved exception list pointer onto stack, creating exception frame\n5. Update FS:[0x0] to point to new exception frame on stack\n6. Set exception marker value (0xffffffff) in stack frame at offset +0x8\n7. Load pExceptionContext parameter from stack offset +0x10\n8. Call DestroyExceptionContext to clean up exception context data structures\n9. Load saved exception list from stack\n10. Restore FS:[0x0] to saved exception list, unwinding exception handler chain\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionContext (void*) - Pointer to exception context structure to clean up\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; callee cleans 4 bytes via __stdcall convention\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Uses Windows SEH (Structured Exception Handling) via FS:[0x0] TIB manipulation.\n  Called from Unwind function at 0x6fc31c93 and 0x6fc31cee during exception unwinding.\n  Callee cleanup (RET 0x4) consistent with __stdcall convention.",
