      "name": "UnlinkExceptionFrameNode",
      "signature": "void UnlinkExceptionFrameNode(ExceptionFrame * pNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Unlinks exception frame node from SEH chain during exception unwinding.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Install exception handler frame to manage SEH chain (FS:[0])\\n2. First unlink iteration:\\n   - Load next pointer from pNode[0]\\n   - If NULL, skip to second iteration\\n   - Load offset/pointer value from pNode[4]\\n   - If offset is negative, convert via bitwise NOT to absolute pointer\\n   - Otherwise calculate relative pointer: pNode + (offset - next[4])\\n   - Write next pointer to calculated target location\\n   - Update next node's offset field with pNode's offset\\n   - Clear pNode[0] and pNode[4] to NULL\\n3. Second unlink iteration (exception-safe re-entrance support):\\n   - Repeat unlink process for safety in exception context\\n4. Restore original SEH chain from saved exception frame\\n\\nParameters:\\n  pNode - Pointer to ExceptionFrame node with:\\n          +0: next pointer (linked list)\\n          +4: offset or absolute pointer value\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void (__stdcall - callee cleans 4-byte parameter)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Offset negative flag (high bit) indicates absolute pointer vs relative\\n  - Bitwise NOT operation converts negative values to absolute addresses\\n  - Dual unlink iterations provide exception-safe cleanup on re-entrance\\n  - Part of VC++ exception handling unwinding infrastructure\\n  - FS:[0] register manages thread-local exception chain on Windows x86\\n  - Called by 20+ exception handlers during destructors and finally blocks\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\n  ExceptionFrame structure (12 bytes):\\n  Offset  Size  Field       Type      Purpose\\n  0x00    4     pNext       void*     Next frame in chain\\n  0x04    4     dwOffset    DWORD     Offset or absolute pointer\\n  0x08    4     dwHandler   DWORD     Exception handler address",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
