      "name": "DeleteCriticalSectionWrapper",
      "signature": "void DeleteCriticalSectionWrapper(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Wrapper function that deletes a critical section object via the Windows API.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Receives implicit CRITICAL_SECTION pointer in EAX register\n2. Pushes the pointer onto the stack as first parameter\n3. Calls the Windows DeleteCriticalSection() API via import table reference\n4. Returns to caller with no value\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT EAX: Pointer to CRITICAL_SECTION structure to delete\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This wrapper adapts implicit EAX parameter convention to Windows __stdcall convention\n- Called exclusively from C++ exception handling (Unwind) functions\n- Used during exception cleanup to properly release synchronization primitives\n- The actual DeleteCriticalSection call is made indirectly through IAT entry at 0x6fc33250\n- Critical section must be initialized before deletion to avoid undefined behavior",
