      "name": "AllocateMessageNode",
      "signature": "ListNode * AllocateMessageNode(void * pListManager, int nTotalSize, uint dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "ListNode *",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a message node for the logging system with optional list insertion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Install SEH exception handler at 0x6ff749e7 to protect allocation operation\n2. OR dwFlags with 0x8 to set allocation control bit\n3. Calculate total allocation size by adding 0x24 bytes to nTotalSize for header overhead\n4. Call AllocateMemory (Ordinal_401) with RTTI type descriptor \".?AUMessage@LogManager@@\", \n   allocation mode -2, and modified flags\n5. If allocation succeeds, initialize ListNode header fields:\n   - Clear pNext pointer at offset +0x0\n   - Clear pPrevOrOffset field at offset +0x4\n6. Store exception state marker 0xFFFFFFFF to indicate completion\n7. If EDI register contains non-NULL list head pointer, insert allocated node into target list \n   by calling InsertListNode\n8. Restore previous SEH exception chain\n9. Return pointer to allocated and initialized message node or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n  pListManager - Pointer to list manager structure base (unused in current implementation)\n  nTotalSize - Size in bytes to allocate for message payload (0x24 bytes added for header)\n  dwFlags - Allocation control flags, will be OR'd with 0x8 before passing to allocator\n  IMPLICIT EDI - Target list head pointer for automatic insertion (NULL to skip insertion)\n\nReturns:\n  Pointer to newly allocated ListNode structure, or NULL if allocation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - dwFlags always OR'd with 0x8 to enable specific allocation behavior\n  - Adds 0x24 bytes overhead to nTotalSize for ListNode header and internal bookkeeping\n  - Uses RTTI descriptor \"szMessageRTTIDescriptor\" (\".?AUMessage@LogManager@@\") for type info\n  - Allocation mode -2 (0xFFFFFFFE) requests specific memory pool behavior\n  - If EDI is NULL on entry, node allocated but not inserted into any list\n  - SEH exception handling protects against allocation failures\n  - Uses InsertListNode with NULL first parameter for standard insertion\n\nStructure Layout (ListNode header):\nOffset | Size | Field Name       | Type           | Description\n-------|------|------------------|----------------|----------------------------------\n0x0    | 4    | pNext            | ListNode *     | Pointer to next node in list\n0x4    | 4    | pPrevOrOffset    | int            | Previous node ptr or offset value\n-------|------|------------------|----------------|----------------------------------\nTotal header size: 8 bytes (message payload follows at +0x8)",
