      "name": "DestroyResourceCollectionsDestructor",
      "signature": "void DestroyResourceCollectionsDestructor(void * this, void * param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "DestroyResourceCollectionsDestructor - Class destructor that deallocates internal resource collections\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EBX and EDI callee-saved registers on stack\n2. Load implicit this pointer from ECX register into EDI\n3. Copy this pointer from EDI to EBX for function call parameter setup\n4. Push parameter 0 (cleanup mode flag) onto stack for ProcessLinkedListElements\n5. Call ProcessLinkedListElements(pResourceContainer, 0) to trigger cleanup callbacks\n6. Call DestroyResourceCollections(pResourceContainer) to deallocate linked list resources\n7. Pop EDI and EBX from stack to restore callee-saved registers\n8. Execute RET to return control to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pResourceContainer (implicit ECX): Pointer to resource container object being destroyed\n    Contains multiple internal resource collections at fixed offsets\n    Collections include linked lists and memory pools requiring cleanup\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; destructor modifies object state and deallocates memory\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Uses __thiscall calling convention with implicit this pointer in ECX register\n  Both helper functions operate on nested data structures within container\n  Function is a class destructor responsible for complete resource cleanup\n  Registers EDI and EBX are preserved as callee-saved across helper function calls",
