      "name": "InitializeVtablePointer",
      "signature": "void InitializeVtablePointer(undefined4 * pObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes secondary object structures with Windows SEH exception handling setup.\n\nThis function completes object initialization by setting up exception handling context,\ninitializing internal collection structures at specific offsets, and preparing the object\nfor use. It is called as the final step in a multi-phase object initialization sequence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current FS:[0x0] exception handler to previousExceptionHandler\n2. Set exceptionHandlerAddress to exception cleanup label (6fe2aed4)\n3. Chain new exception handler: set FS:[0x0] to point to previousExceptionHandler variable\n4. Set exceptionState = 1 as initial phase marker\n5. Call InitializeFirstSubstructure (FUN_6fe11880) with parameter 1\n6. Set exceptionState to 0x00000000 (& 0xffffff00) to clear lowest byte\n7. Call InitializeSecondSubstructure (FUN_6fe11500) at offset +0x14 from pObject\n8. Set exceptionState = 0xffffffff indicating final phase\n9. Call InitializeThirdSubstructure (FUN_6fe11920) at offset +0x4 from pObject\n10. Restore previous exception handler from stack to FS:[0x0]\n11. Return with callee cleanup (fastcall convention)\n\nParameters:\npObject - Pointer to object structure being initialized; expects object with:\n          Offset +0x00: virtual function table pointer\n          Offset +0x04: first substructure needing initialization\n          Offset +0x14: second substructure needing initialization\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Windows SEH exception handling chain setup/restore for safe initialization\n- exceptionState values: 1 (first init phase), 0 (second init phase), 0xffffffff (final)\n- Uses __fastcall convention with pObject in ECX register\n- Each sub-initialization function called with relevant offset address\n- Exception handler ensures cleanup on error during initialization",
