      "name": "UnwindExceptionFrameNode",
      "signature": "void UnwindExceptionFrameNode(ExceptionFrame * pExceptionFrame)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Unwinds an exception frame by relinking its node back into the exception handler chain.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save FS:[0] exception handler pointer in pPrevExceptionChain for restoration\n2. Initialize unwinding status flag (dwUnwindingStatus = 0)\n3. Temporarily replace FS:[0] with address of pPrevExceptionChain variable to create SEH frame\n4. Call ProcessExceptionListNodes() to process any pending list cleanup operations\n5. Set dwUnwindingStatus = 0xFFFFFFFF to indicate unwinding is in progress\n6. Load next exception handler pointer from pExceptionFrame->next_handler (offset +4)\n7. Test if next_handler is null: if null, skip to cleanup phase (0x6fbf4585)\n8. Load offset_value from pExceptionFrame->offset_value (offset +8)\n9. Test sign bit of offset_value: if negative, apply bitwise NOT to decode pointer\n10. If offset_value positive: calculate node address = (frame+4 - next_handler->next) + offset_value\n11. If offset_value negative: use negated value directly as node pointer\n12. Unlink: write next_handler to calculated node pointer (relink operation)\n13. Load handler pointer from pExceptionFrame->next_handler (offset +4)\n14. Load next pointer from pExceptionFrame->offset_value (offset +8)\n15. Update previous handler's next pointer: *(handler+4) = next_pointer\n16. Clear pExceptionFrame->next_handler (set to 0)\n17. Clear pExceptionFrame->offset_value (set to 0)\n18. Restore previous exception chain: FS:[0] = pPrevExceptionChain (via automated SEH unwind)\n19. Return to caller (stdcall: caller pops 4-byte parameter)\n\nParameters:\npExceptionFrame (ExceptionFrame*): Pointer to exception frame containing:\n  Offset +0x0: Reserved field\n  Offset +0x4: Pointer to next exception handler node in chain\n  Offset +0x8: Encoded offset or pointer value for relinking calculation\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Exception handler chain updated as side effect.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles negative offset values (stored as bitwise NOT of actual address)\n- Handles null handler pointers safely (branches to cleanup without processing)\n- Uses SEH structured exception handling for exception chain frame setup\n- Offset calculation handles both positive (calculate from frame location) and negative (decoded address) encodings\n- Automatic unwinding restores exception handler chain via SEH frame cleanup\n- Uses FS:[0] TEB exception chain for compatibility with Windows SEH\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name      Type       Description\n0x0     4     reserved        uint       Reserved for future use\n0x4     4     next_handler    void*      Pointer to next exception handler in chain\n0x8     4     offset_value    int        Encoded offset (negative) or calculated offset (positive)\n0xC     -     (end)           -          Total structure size: 12 bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
