      "name": "DestroyResourceCollections",
      "signature": "void DestroyResourceCollections(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Destroys all linked list resources associated with a game state object.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Preserve ESI register on stack\n2. Load first hash chunk object pointer from pGameState+0x40\n3. Test pointer for NULL or negative value (list termination check)\n4. If list empty, jump to AURGN collection processing\n5. Call UnlinkListNodeFromCollection to invoke destructor on current chunk\n6. Call DeallocateMemoryBlock with hash chunk type ID and refcount -2\n7. Reload next pointer from pGameState+0x40 (follow linked list chain)\n8. Repeat until entire hash chunk collection exhausted\n9. Load first AURGN object pointer from pGameState+0x30\n10. Test pointer for NULL or negative value (list termination check)\n\nParameters:\n  pGameState: Pointer to game state container with resource lists\n    - Offset +0x40: First hash object chunk pointer\n    - Offset +0x30: First AURGN object pointer\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value, performs in-place destruction\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Both collections are singly-linked lists terminating on pointer <= 0\n  - Hash chunks destroyed first, then AURGN objects\n  - Used during game shutdown sequence",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:4639679c8d3a53299d8b9a9e761b0107",
