      "name": "AllocateEntityId",
      "signature": "uint AllocateEntityId(void * pUnused, void * pEntityTable)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Allocates a new entity ID from the entity hash table\n\nIncrements a global counter and searches the hash table to find an available slot\nby probing for hash collisions. Returns a unique entity identifier for creating new\ngame entities (units, items, etc.) without conflicts.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Increment counter at pEntityTable+0x48\n2. If counter wraps to 0, set overflow flag at pEntityTable+0x4c to 1, then retry\n3. Check if overflow flag at pEntityTable+0x4c is set; exit with 0 if not set\n4. Calculate hash bucket: (counter & hash_mask) where hash_mask is at pEntityTable+0x24\n5. Get hash table base from pEntityTable+0x1c\n6. Load first node from bucket at base + (hash_result * 3 * 4 + 8)\n7. If first node is null or invalid, return current counter value\n8. Iterate through linked list of hash nodes at offset +0x4\n9. For each node, compare node ID at offset 0 with current counter\n10. If ID matches, loop back to increment counter again (ID already in use)\n11. If no match found in list, return current counter as allocated ID\n\nParameters:\n  unused - Reserved parameter (passed in ECX, unused)\n  pEntityTable - Pointer to entity table structure\n    +0x1c: Pointer to hash table array\n    +0x24: Hash mask (AND mask for modulo operation)\n    +0x48: Current entity counter (incremented each call)\n    +0x4c: Table-ready flag (set on overflow, cleared externally)\n\nReturns:\n  EAX - New unique entity ID (uint)\n  Always returns non-zero value (counter starts at 1)\n  Returns immediately if table-ready flag is 0\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Counter never returns 0; after overflow wraps to 1\n  - Collision detection via hash table linked list traversal\n  - Table must be initialized with valid pointers before use\n  - Assumes hash buckets are initialized with valid node links",
