      "name": "SearchHashTableForNode",
      "signature": "void * SearchHashTableForNode(void * pHashTable, uint dwSearchValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Searches a hash table for a node matching the given search value.\n\nALGORITHM\n1. Load hash mask from pHashTable[0x24] to mask the search value\n2. Hash the dwSearchValue using the mask to find initial bucket index\n3. Load bucket array base address from pHashTable[0x1c]\n4. Calculate bucket offset using (hash_value * 3 * 4) addressing\n5. Load initial node pointer from calculated bucket position + 0x4\n6. If node pointer is null or invalid, return NULL\n7. Compare node value with search value at offset [nodePointer]\n8. If values match, return node pointer\n9. Calculate next node index using hash collision chain\n10. Load next node pointer from chain offset + initial node offset\n11. Repeat comparison loop until node found or chain exhausted\n12. Return NULL if node not found\n\nPARAMETERS\npHashTable: void * - Pointer to hash table structure with bucket array and mask\ndwSearchValue: uint - The node value to search for in the table\n\nRETURNS\nvoid * - Pointer to matching node if found, NULL (0x0) if not found\n\nSPECIAL CASES\nNull pointer checks at multiple points to handle empty buckets and chain termination\nHash collision handling via next pointer chain traversal\nBitwise AND masking used to mask out invalid pointer flags",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
