      "name": "ReallocateEntityPoolStorage",
      "signature": "void ReallocateEntityPoolStorage(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Reallocates and reorganizes entity pool storage while preserving slot data.\n\nExpands or shrinks a dynamic entity pool by reallocating the underlying slot\narray, initializing newly allocated slots with proper constructors, and cleaning\nup removed slots with proper destructors. Uses a two-phase allocation strategy:\nattempt in-place realloc first, and fall back to malloc+copy if realloc fails.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load old slot array pointer from pPoolManager[2]\n2. If shrinking (targetSlotCount < currentSlotCount):\n   a. Loop through slots from targetSlotCount to currentSlotCount\n   b. Call ExecuteWithExceptionHandler for each slot to trigger destructors\n3. Update pPoolManager[0] with new slot count\n4. Attempt realloc on existing buffer (preserves data in-place):\n   a. Call AllocateOrReallocateMemory with old buffer pointer\n   b. If realloc succeeds, update pPoolManager[2] and exit\n5. If realloc failed (NULL returned), use malloc path:\n   a. Allocate new buffer via AllocateMemoryFromArena\n   b. Update pPoolManager[2] with new buffer\n   c. Copy and initialize slots from old to new buffer:\n      - Calculate copy count as min(targetSlotCount, currentSlotCount)\n      - Loop through slots, calling InitializePoolSlotLink for each\n      - Call ExecuteWithExceptionHandler for slot initialization\n   d. Free old buffer via DeallocateMemoryBlock\n6. Return (function modifies pool structure in-place)\n\nParameters:\n  pPoolManager [4 bytes]: Pointer to pool manager structure with fields:\n    [0] = current slot count (dword)\n    [4] = max slot count (dword) \n    [8] = pointer to slot array (PoolSlotLink *)\n  targetSlotCount [4 bytes]: Target number of slots to allocate\n\nReturns:\n  void - modifies pPoolManager structure in-place, specifically pPoolManager[2]\n         with new slot array pointer after reallocation\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Slot stride: 0xc bytes (3 dwords per PoolSlotLink structure)\n  - Realloc address: 0x6fbf3448 (calls AllocateOrReallocateMemory with RTTI)\n  - Malloc address: 0x6fbf345d (calls AllocateMemoryFromArena)\n  - Free address: 0x6fbf34a8 (calls DeallocateMemoryBlock for old buffer)\n  - Type descriptor: g_szTSExplicitListURGNTypeDescriptor (0x6fc41bc0)\n  - Flags value: 0x10 (used in allocation calls)\n  - Allocation index: -2 (used in allocation calls)\n  \nStructure Layout - PoolSlotLink (stride 0xc bytes):\n  Offset | Size | Field        | Type     | Description\n  -------|------|--------------|----------|---------------------------\n  0x0    | 4    | field_0      | dword    | Slot state/link field 1\n  0x4    | 4    | field_4      | dword    | Slot state/link field 2\n  0x8    | 4    | field_8      | dword    | Slot state/link field 3",
