      "name": "ReleaseLockForTypeinfo",
      "signature": "void ReleaseLockForTypeinfo(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Releases the critical section lock protecting type_info object state.\n\nThis function is a thin wrapper around LeaveCriticalSectionByIndex that\nreleases a specific critical section lock used by the type_info system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push immediate lock index 0xe (14) onto the stack as function argument\n2. Call LeaveCriticalSectionByIndex(0xe) to release the critical section\n3. Clean up stack with POP ECX (stdcall calling convention requirement)\n4. Execute RET instruction to return control to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - The lock index (0xe) is passed as an immediate constant value,\nnot as a parameter from the caller. This is a fixed lock index that\nalways protects type_info object access synchronization.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns no value, it only performs the lock release.\n\nSpecial Cases:\nLock index 0xe is reserved for type_info object synchronization and must\nbe released when type_info objects are destroyed. Failure to properly\nrelease this lock could cause deadlocks or resource leaks.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:3b81466ebb016fe07b13b68f44a18bd2e7ab1cf39e3b34b0563a6b92cce1c0ca",
