      "name": "WriteStringToBuffer",
      "signature": "undefined WriteStringToBuffer(int charCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Writes repeated characters or string data to a buffered output stream.\n\nThis function is called during printf-style formatting to output formatted strings and\npadding characters. It checks buffer flags and counts before delegating to\nWriteCharToFileBuffer for actual character output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check output state flags at pState+0xc for buffering mode (0x40 = _IOFBF)\n2. Check pState+0x8 for error condition flag\n3. If buffering mode disabled OR error flag set: Add charCount to counter and exit\n4. Otherwise: Loop for each character count from charCount down to 1\n   a. If charCount < 1: Exit loop\n   b. Decrement charCount\n   c. Call WriteCharToFileBuffer to output character at ESI to pFile\n   d. Check if WriteCharToFileBuffer returned EOF (-1)\n   e. If EOF: Break loop and return error status\n\nParameters:\n  charCount (int) - Number of characters to write (passed on stack)\n  charValue (uchar, implicit in ESI) - Character byte to output (unaffected register)\n  pFile (FILE*, implicit in EBX) - Output FILE stream structure (unaffected register)\n  pState (int, implicit in EDI) - State structure with flags/counts (unaffected register)\n  pCharCount (int*, implicit return addr) - Pointer to character counter (unaffected register)\n\nReturns:\n  int - Final character count from accumulator or count after adding charCount\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If FILE stream not in buffered mode: Just increments counter without calling WriteCharToFileBuffer\n  - If error flag set in pState+0x8: Bypasses output and updates counter\n  - EOF (-1) from WriteCharToFileBuffer terminates the write loop immediately\n  - Uses implicit register parameters following custom calling convention pattern",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
