      "name": "InitializeModuleWithValidation",
      "signature": "void InitializeModuleWithValidation(void * pModuleBase)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Validates module structure and performs conditional initialization.\n\nValidates that the input module pointer is non-null and initializes module fields.\nIf module pointer is null, logs error and calls exit(). Otherwise, checks optional\nfield at offset 0xc and conditionally initializes it before performing final\nmodule initialization. Used in module startup sequence to ensure proper initialization\nor graceful failure with diagnostic information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if input module pointer (ESI/pModuleBase) is null\n2. If null: Get return address, log error with file/line info, and exit program\n3. If valid: Load optional field pointer from [module_base + 0xc]\n4. If optional field exists: Call InitializeModule with code 0x35\n5. Call InitializeModule with code 0x38 and module pointer\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pModuleBase: Pointer to module structure to initialize. If null, triggers \n              error handler. Field at offset 0xc is optional initialization flag.\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function does not return if module is invalid (calls exit). Otherwise \n       returns after initialization complete.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Null module pointer: Error logged at LRUCache.cpp line 49 (code 0x31), \n    then program exits with exit(-1)\n  - Optional field at +0xc: If present, additional initialization occurs\n  - Error handling: Uses GetReturnAddress for stack unwinding context",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
