      "name": "InitializeEntityResource",
      "signature": "byte * InitializeEntityResource(void * this, EntityCollection * pEntityCollection, int entityTypeID, LPSTR outputPathBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "byte *",
      "comment": "Initializes an entity resource by allocating cache memory, copying entity data, and configuring network parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Serialize entity data from collection\n2. If serialization succeeds, lookup entity in hash table cache\n3. If not in cache, retrieve entity file path and create new hash entry\n4. Allocate cache node (0xa0 bytes) for entity data\n5. Zero-initialize the entire cache buffer (48 dwords)\n6. Copy entity descriptor string to buffer offset 0xa0\n7. Check entity flag at offset +0x44 to determine initialization path\n8. If flag clear (0), initialize network session and configure resource array:\n   - Set resource array base to DAT_6fe883a0\n   - Validate array count does not exceed 0x20\n   - Copy resource entries from global data table\n   - Store default resource count at array end\n9. If flag set (1), initialize network configuration and set error flag if needed\n10. Return pointer to initialized resource buffer or NULL on error\n\nParameters:\n- pEntityCollection: Pointer to entity collection context (implicit this in ECX)\n- entityTypeID: Entity type identifier (stack parameter)\n- outputPathBuffer: Output buffer for file path (stack parameter)\n\nReturns:\n- byte*: Pointer to initialized resource buffer on success\n- NULL: If any initialization step fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Serialization returns 0: Function returns NULL immediately\n- Entity flag at offset 0x44 bit 0 clear: Uses network session path\n- Entity flag at offset 0x44 bit 0 set: Uses network configuration path\n- Array overflow (count * stride > 0x4000): Error code 0x44d\n- Array size > 0x20: Error code 0x452\n- Cache allocation failures: Error codes 0x41c or 0x421",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
