      "signature": "uint FindFirstSetBitPosition(uint bitmask)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Finds the position of the first set bit in a 32-bit value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if the input bitmask is zero and return 0 immediately if so\n2. Initialize bit position counter to 0\n3. Loop through each bit position, checking if the bit at that position is set\n4. Increment position counter until a set bit is found\n5. Return the 1-based bit position (bitPosition + 1)\n\nParameters:\n  bitmask (uint) - 32-bit value to search for the first set bit\n\nReturns:\n  uint - 1-based position of first set bit (1-32), or 0 if input is zero\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Input of 0 returns 0 immediately (cannot search for bit position in zero)\n  - Maximum return value is 32 (highest possible bit in 32-bit integer)\n  - Uses 1-based indexing (bit 0 returns 1, bit 31 returns 32)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
