      "name": "SpillFpuStackForClassify",
      "signature": "uint SpillFpuStackForClassify(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Spills FPU stack registers ST0 and ST1 to memory for FP classification.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocates 0x2c bytes of stack space\n2. Stores ST0 as 80-bit extended double at [ESP]\n3. Stores ST1 as 80-bit extended double at [ESP+0xc]\n4. Calls FP classification function with spilled values\n5. Cleans up stack and returns classification result\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ST0 - first floating-point value to classify\n- IMPLICIT: ST1 - second floating-point value to classify\n\nReturns:\n- Classification result from inner function (FP exception type or 0)\n\nNotes:\n- Used by float/double special value checks (infinity, NaN detection)\n- Callers check FPU status word (0x3800 mask) and IEEE 754 exponent bits",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
