      "name": "DivideFloatWithFpuMarshaling",
      "signature": "undefined4 DivideFloatWithFpuMarshaling(uint param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Performs floating-point division with FPU operand marshaling for edge cases.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent bits from IEEE 754 float using mask 0x7F800000\n2. If exponent equals 0x7F800000 (NaN or Infinity), perform direct FDIV and return\n3. Check FPU status word bits 11-13 (0x3800) for stack top pointer state\n4. If FPU stack is non-empty, load divisor and call MarshalFpuOperandsForDivision\n5. Otherwise, save current FPU value to extended double temp, load divisor, \n   call MarshalFpuOperandsForDivision, then restore saved value and return\n\nParameters:\n  dwFloatBits (dword) - IEEE 754 single precision float as raw bits for exponent check\n  IMPLICIT: ST(0) - FPU dividend value\n  IMPLICIT: ST(1) - May contain value to preserve during marshaling\n\nReturns:\n  dword - Result in EAX (float value after FDIV operation via FPU)\n  IMPLICIT: ST(0) - Division result on FPU stack\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x7F800000 - IEEE 754 single precision exponent mask (bits 23-30)\n  0x3800     - FPU status word TOP field mask (bits 11-13, stack pointer)\n\nStructure Layout (Stack Frame):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type     Description\n  -0x10   10    ldTempFpuValue     float10  Temporary extended double storage\n  +0x04   4     dwFloatBits        dword    Input float as raw bits\n  +0x08   4     [return address]   dword    Caller return address\n\nNote: ldTempFpuValue is a phantom variable (assembly-only, not in decompiled code)\nused to preserve FPU ST(0) during operand marshaling when FPU stack is empty.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
