      "name": "PerformExtendedDivision",
      "signature": "undefined4 PerformExtendedDivision(undefined4 param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Performs extended precision floating-point division with special value handling.\n\nDivides the value in FPU ST0 (dividend) by the double-precision divisor passed on\nthe stack. Handles IEEE 754 special cases (Inf/NaN) and FPU exception states by\nrouting to appropriate processing paths.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent bits from divisor high DWORD to check for special values\n2. If divisor is Inf/NaN (exponent = 0x7FF), perform direct FDIVR and return\n3. Check FPU status word for pending exceptions (precision control bits 0x3800)\n4. If exceptions pending: load divisor and call ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision\n5. If no exceptions: save ST1 to stack, load divisor, call division routine, restore ST1\n\nParameters:\n  dwDivisorLo (uint): Low 32 bits of IEEE 754 double-precision divisor\n  dwDivisorHi (uint): High 32 bits of divisor (sign + exponent + high mantissa)\n  IMPLICIT ST0: Dividend value in FPU register (extended precision)\n  IMPLICIT ST1: May contain value to preserve during division\n\nReturns:\n  ST0: Result of division (dividend / divisor)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Divisor is Inf: Returns 0 (x/Inf = 0)\n  - Divisor is NaN: Returns NaN (x/NaN = NaN)\n  - FPU exceptions pending: Handled via ProcessExtendedPrecisionDivision\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x7ff00000 - IEEE 754 double exponent mask (bits 52-62)\n  0x3800     - FPU status word exception flags mask (C0, C2, C3)\n  0xc        - Size of extended precision temp (12 bytes aligned)\n\nStack Layout (after PUSH EAX):\n  [ESP+0x04] = dwDivisorLo (low DWORD of double)\n  [ESP+0x08] = dwDivisorHi (high DWORD of double)\n  [ESP+0x0C] = Return address",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
