      "comment": "Computes the IEEE 754 extended precision (80-bit) floating-point remainder.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate exponent ranges using lookup table to detect special cases\n2. Check for infinity (exponent 0x7FFF) and zero conditions\n3. If exponent difference > 63, use iterative subtraction with scaling\n4. Otherwise, use FPREM instruction directly for remainder calculation\n5. Apply sign preservation from original dividend\n\nParameters:\n  dwMantissaLow  [uint]   - Low 32 bits of 64-bit mantissa\n  dwMantissaHigh [uint]   - High 32 bits of mantissa (bits 32-63)\n  wExponentSign  [ushort] - 15-bit exponent + sign bit (bit 15)\n  IMPLICIT: Second operand passed via stack at ESP+0x1C..0x30\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Passthrough of EAX register (actual result in ST0 FPU register)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns unchanged if either operand is infinity (exp=0x7FFF)\n  - Returns unchanged if divisor is zero\n  - Uses FPREM for small exponent differences\n  - Uses iterative subtraction for large exponent differences\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x7FFF - Maximum exponent (infinity/NaN indicator)\n  0x8000 - Sign bit mask\n  0x7800 - High nibble of exponent for table lookup\n  0x3F   - Maximum exponent difference for direct FPREM\n  0x0A   - Threshold for iterative reduction loop\n\nStructure Layout (80-bit Extended Float on Stack):\n  Offset  Size  Field         Type    Description\n  0x00    4     MantissaLow   uint    Bits 0-31 of significand\n  0x04    4     MantissaHigh  uint    Bits 32-63 of significand\n  0x08    2     ExponentSign  ushort  15-bit exp + sign bit",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
