      "comment": "Unwraps and dequeues a list node from the active list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load list node pointer from stack parameter at [EBP - 0x10]\n2. Add 0x4 to pointer to access the dequeue member/field\n3. Jump to UnlinkListNode for dequeue operation\n\nParameters:\n  pListNode (void *): Pointer to list node structure to unwind/dequeue\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value. List node is dequeued as side effect.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  This is a thunk function that wraps UnlinkListNode with parameter adjustment.\n  The offset adjustment (+0x4) suggests the node has an embedded dequeue structure\n  at offset 0x4 from the node base address.\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name     Type    Description\n  ------  ----  ----------     ----    -----------\n  0x0     4     (base)         void*   Node base pointer\n  0x4     N/A   dequeueNode    struct  Dequeue list node member\n\nRelated Functions:\n  UnlinkListNode: Core dequeue operation called via tail call at 0x6fc31b20",
