      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Exception unwinding return address adjustment thunk for C++ exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the return address from the stack (stored at [EBP + 4])\n2. Add 0x50 (80 decimal) bytes to the return address to adjust the unwind location\n3. Jump to DeleteCriticalSectionWrapper for cleanup and continuation\n\nParameters:\nNone. The return address is implicitly accessed via the stack frame.\n\nReturns:\nDoes not return directly. Jumps to cleanup_delete_critical_section after adjusting the return address.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- This function is part of C++ structured exception handling (SEH) machinery\n- Used in exception unwinding to skip over stack frames and adjust control flow\n- Referenced from exception handling tables (likely part of .pdata/.xdata sections)\n- The 0x50 byte adjustment may represent skipping a particular stack frame size or exception handling block",
