      "name": "UnlinkListNodeThunk",
      "signature": "void UnlinkListNodeThunk(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Thunk wrapper that unlinks a list node from a doubly-linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load list node pointer from stack parameter into EAX register\n2. Jump to UnlinkListNode function with node pointer as parameter\n3. UnlinkListNode removes the node from the doubly-linked list by:\n   - Updating the previous node's forward pointer to skip the current node\n   - Updating the next node's backward pointer to skip the current node\n   - Clearing the current node's forward and backward pointers\n\nParameters:\n  pListNode (Stack[0x4], 4 bytes): Pointer to doubly-linked list node structure\n    - Offset +0: Pointer to previous node\n    - Offset +4: Signed offset or pointer to next node (negative = bitwise NOT, positive = offset)\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - This is a minimal thunk function that delegates all work to UnlinkListNode\n  - Used in exception handling contexts (referenced from data table)\n  - The LEA instruction loads from [EBP - 0x14], suggesting this is called from functions\n    with local list nodes at that stack offset\n  - The jump to UnlinkListNode is a tail call optimization\n\nStack Layout (relative to EBP):\n  EBP+0x4: Return address\n  EBP-0x14: Address of list node to unlink (passed as parameter)",
