      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes C++ exception handling context by wrapping a delegated operation\nin a Structured Exception Handling (SEH) frame.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load exception context pointer from function parameter\n2. Push pointer to local stack frame to create exception handler structure\n3. Call ExecuteWithExceptionHandler to install SEH frame and delegate processing\n4. Return to caller with __stdcall parameter cleanup\n\nParameters:\npExceptionContext (void*): Pointer to exception handling context structure containing\ninitialization state and linkage information. Passed through to\nExecuteWithExceptionHandler for SEH frame setup.\n\nReturns:\nvoid: Function returns normally after delegated operation completes. Exception\nhandling is managed by installed SEH frame in ExecuteWithExceptionHandler.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Wrapper for exception safety: Creates exception context on local stack\n- Uses __stdcall convention with 4-byte parameter cleanup (RET 0x4)\n- Part of C++ exception handling mechanism for stack unwinding during errors\n- Local stack variable at [EBP - 0x18] serves as exception context parameter",
