      "name": "DestroyAURGNObject",
      "signature": "void DestroyAURGNObject(void * pObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Destructor for AURGN game object. Coordinates cleanup of exception handling context and deallocation of the object's memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize exception handling context by calling InitializeAURGNDestructor\n2. Call DeallocateMemoryBlock (Ordinal_403) with AURGN type identifier and destructor flag (-2)\n3. Return to caller with stack cleanup (callee-cleanup __stdcall)\n\nParameters:\npObject: void* - Pointer to the AURGN object being destroyed\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns to caller via RET 0x4 (callee cleans 4 bytes from stack)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type identifier: g_szAURGNTypeID (MANGLED_AURGN_NAME = \".?AURGN@@\")\n- Destructor flag: -2 indicates object destruction context\n- Exception handling: Managed through InitializeAURGNDestructor before calling main destructor\n- Calling convention: __stdcall (callee-cleanup, RET 0x4)",
