      "name": "DeallocateEntityCollectionCleanup",
      "signature": "void DeallocateEntityCollectionCleanup(EntityCollection * pEntityCollection)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Deallocate entity collection and cleanup all contained entities with exception handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save ESI register to stack\n2. Save EDI register to stack\n3. Load entity count from pEntityCollection->entityCount (offset +0x4)\n4. Initialize entity index (EDI) to 0\n5. If entity count <= 0, jump to cleanup array pointer\n6. Loop through entities with stride 0x38 bytes:\n   a. Load entity array base from pEntityCollection->pEntityArray (offset +0x8)\n   b. Calculate current entity pointer: pEntityArray + (entityIndex * 0x38)\n   c. Call UnlinkEntityStructuresWithExceptionHandler to unlink entity structures\n   d. Increment entity index (EDI)\n   e. Add 0x38 to offset (EBX)\n   f. Compare entity index with count\n   g. Jump back to loop start if more entities\n7. Load entity array pointer from pEntityCollection->pEntityArray (offset +0x8)\n8. Test if array pointer is non-null\n9. If array pointer is null, jump to function exit\n10. Call DeallocateMemoryBlock with parameters:\n    - pEntityArray: Entity array pointer\n    - Type: RTTI type reference (0x6fe3417c)\n    - Cookie: -2 (0xfffffffe) deallocation marker\n    - Flags: 0 (no flags)\n11. Restore EDI register from stack\n12. Restore ESI register from stack\n13. Return with stack cleanup\n\nParameters:\n- pEntityCollection (EntityCollection *): Pointer to EntityCollection structure containing:\n  - offset +0x4: entityCount (uint) - Number of entities in array\n  - offset +0x8: pEntityArray (void *) - Pointer to entity array\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function returns with no value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention\n- Magic number 0x38: Entity stride size (56 bytes per entity)\n- Magic number 0x2c: Offset within entity to list node for unlinking\n- Magic number 0xfffffffe (-2): Deallocation cookie for memory deallocation\n- If entityCount is 0, loop is skipped but memory deallocation still occurs if pEntityArray is valid\n- Exception handler frame setup ensures cleanup completes even on exceptions\n- RTTI type reference 0x6fe3417c used for C++ exception-safe deallocation\n\nStructure Layout:\nEntityCollection:\nOffset Size Field Name   Type  Description\n0x0    4    field_0      uint  Unknown field\n0x4    4    entityCount  uint  Number of entities in array\n0x8    4    pEntityArray void* Pointer to entity array\n0xc    N    (padding)    -     Additional fields if any",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
