      "name": "WriteErrorMessage",
      "signature": "void WriteErrorMessage(int nErrorCode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Display runtime error message to console or message box.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load stack guard cookie (0x6fc406bc) and XOR with EBP for validation\n2. Look up error code in error code lookup table (0x6fc40490) using linear search\n3. If code not found (index >= 0x13), skip to cleanup and return\n4. Check output mode flags (0x6fc42470 and 0x6fc42474) to determine output destination\n5. If flag 1 (0x6fc42470 == 1) or flag 2 (0x6fc42474 == 1) set, use alternate output path\n6. Get module path from GetModuleFileNameA API (0x6fc331f4)\n7. Build error message by concatenating: \"[module_path] Error code: [error_string]\"\n8. If message buffer exceeds 60 bytes, truncate to last 59 chars of path\n9. Allocate output buffer (aligned to 4 bytes) and concatenate all strings\n10. Display message via ___crtMessageBoxA with MB_ICONEXCLAMATION (0x12010) flag\n11. Verify stack guard cookie matches before return (anti-stack-corruption check)\n\nParameters:\n  errorCode (int): The error code to look up and display (values 0x02, 0x08, 0x09, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Error code 0xFC is handled as invalid (line 6fbf9c08)\n  - Message truncation at 60-char path length limit (0x3c)\n  - Alternate output path (0x6fbf9cd6) for flag 1 or flag 2 set\n  - Stack guard validation at function exit (VerifyStackCanary at 0x6fbf9d0c)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Error Code Table (0x6fc40490):\n    Offset  Size  Content           Type        Description\n    +0x00   4     Code values       DWORD       Error code 0x02, 0x08, 0x09, etc.\n    +0x04   4     Message pointers  DWORD*      Points to error message strings\n    (Stride: 8 bytes per entry, 0x13 max entries)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:f8f89093f5c5a57c3cdd998b61227276",
