      "name": "ProcessAllNodeItems",
      "signature": "int ProcessAllNodeItems(void * pCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Iterates through all items in a global node list and executes a callback function for each item.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input callback pointer is not null; return 0 if null\n2. Load global root pointer from DAT_6fe88328\n3. Check if global root is valid; skip processing if null\n4. For each node in the linked list:\n   a. Load node's item start pointer from offset +0x104\n   b. Load item count from offset +0x10c\n   c. Initialize item counter to 0\n   d. If item count > 0, iterate through all items:\n      - Calculate item address as (base + index * 0x60)\n      - Call callback function with item pointer\n      - Increment total processed count and item index\n      - Continue until all items processed\n   e. Load next node pointer from offset +0x10c\n   f. Continue until no more nodes exist\n5. Return total count of items processed in EAX\n\nParameters:\npCallback: Pointer to callback function to execute for each item. Function is called with no parameters and ignores return value. Called via indirect call at offset +0x18 relative to current stack frame.\n\nReturns:\nEAX: Total count of items processed (int). Returns 0 if callback is null or global root is null.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty node list: Returns 0\n- Null callback: Returns 0 immediately without processing\n- Items stored with 0x60 byte stride within each node\n- Uses EBP as accumulator for processed item count\n- Callback invocation uses register-indirect call pattern",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0b2e60eba79ec96baa9f6f92bf54c7aa",
