      "name": "ResetModuleLinkedList",
      "signature": "void ResetModuleLinkedList(void * pContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Resets all modules in a linked list and clears global module state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global module list head from DAT_6fe88328\n2. If list is empty (NULL), skip to cleanup\n3. For each node in the linked list:\n   a. Load next node pointer from current node + 0x10c\n   b. Load array pointer from current node + 0x104\n   c. Call ResetNestedArrayStructures to reset the array\n   d. Clear array pointer (offset 0x104) to NULL\n   e. Load function pointer from current node + 0x108\n   f. Call FUN_6fe22d30 to process the function pointer\n   g. Clear function pointer (offset 0x108) to NULL\n   h. Call InitializeModule with code 0x2a to reinitialize module state\n   i. Move to next node and continue loop\n4. Clear global module list head to NULL\n5. Return\n\nNode Structure (inferred):\n  Offset  Size  Field        Type      Description\n  ------  ----  -----------  --------  -----------------------\n  0x104   4     pArrayPtr    void*     Pointer to nested array\n  0x108   4     pFuncPtr     void*     Function pointer\n  0x10c   4     pNextNode    Node*     Pointer to next node\n\nParameters:\n  pContext (ECX) - Context pointer passed to ResetNestedArrayStructures\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty list: Returns immediately without processing\n  - Global state: Clears DAT_6fe88328 to prevent further access\n  - Module code 0x2a: Appears to be module initialization/reset code\n  - Unaffected EDI: EDI register is preserved through loop iterations\n\nNotes:\n  - Function uses __fastcall convention with context in ECX\n  - Linked list is modified in-place by clearing pointers\n  - Called from Ordinal_10089 during module cleanup phase",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
