      "name": "CopyMemoryToGameBuffer",
      "signature": "void CopyMemoryToGameBuffer(undefined4 * sourceBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Copies 64 dwords from source buffer to game buffer.\n\nThis function copies exactly 64 32-bit values (256 bytes) from the provided source buffer to a fixed destination buffer in the game's data segment (0x6fe87df0). After the copy completes, it sets a completion flag (0x6fe88324) to 1, indicating that the buffer copy operation has finished. This is likely used for initializing or updating critical game state data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store ESI register to preserve it (callee-save requirement)\n2. Retrieve sourceBuffer pointer from stack parameter (ESP + 8)\n3. Preserve EDI register  \n4. Initialize copy counter ECX to 0x40 (64 decimal)\n5. Load destination address EDI to 0x6fe87df0 (game buffer)\n6. Execute MOVSD.REP instruction to copy ESI to EDI 64 times\n7. Restore EDI register\n8. Set completion flag at 0x6fe88324 to value 1\n9. Restore ESI register\n10. Return and clean up 4 bytes from stack\n\nParameters:\nsourceBuffer (undefined4*) - Pointer to source data buffer containing 64 dwords to copy\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; side effects include populating the game buffer and setting the completion flag.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Fixed destination address 0x6fe87df0: This buffer is part of the game's global data and is always the target\n- Fixed copy size (64 dwords): Hardcoded in the ECX register initialization\n- Completion flag 0x6fe88324: Set to 1 after every copy operation\n- Calling convention __stdcall: Callee cleans up 4-byte parameter from stack (RET 0x4)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ebaaf5672e72e8d48014f357d4174d80",
