      "name": "GetClosestColorIndex",
      "signature": "byte GetClosestColorIndex(byte red, byte green, byte blue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Finds the closest matching color index in the active palette using weighted distance calculation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize minDistance to 0x7fffffff (max value) and bestMatchIndex to 0\n2. Load palette bounds from global data (DAT_6fe875ec for max count, DAT_6fe87ef0 for start)\n3. Return 0 if palette start index exceeds max count (invalid palette state)\n4. For each palette entry from start to max:\n   a. Check if entry is valid (DAT_6fe88324 flag or DAT_6fe87df0 marker)\n   b. Check for exact match (DAT_6fe8831c holds 24-bit target color)\n   c. If exact match found, return 0 immediately\n   d. Load base color components from table at offsets +0x1a, +0x19, +0x18 (indexed by paletteIndex*4)\n   e. Calculate differences: red - base_red, green - base_green, blue - base_blue\n   f. Use difference values as indices into DAT_6fe879f0 distance lookup table\n   g. Sum three distance values to get total distance metric\n   h. If total distance < minDistance, update minDistance and bestMatchIndex\n   i. Increment paletteIndex and continue until palette exhausted\n5. Return bestMatchIndex as final result (masked to byte)\n\nParameters:\n  red (byte) - Red component of target color (0-255)\n  green (byte) - Green component of target color (0-255)\n  blue (byte) - Blue component of target color (0-255)\n\nReturns:\n  byte - Index (0-255) of the palette entry with minimum color distance, or 0 for exact match or invalid palette\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns 0 if palette start index > max count (bounds check failure)\n  - Returns 0 if exact match found in active palette\n  - Uses lookup table at DAT_6fe879f0 for weighted distance calculation\n  - Palette entry validity determined by DAT_6fe88324 condition or non-zero marker in DAT_6fe87df0\n  - Always returns byte-masked result even though intermediate calculations use 32-bit values",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:431913c3dc4ef64587148c41d9a7931e",
