      "name": "StoreByteSwappedColorValue",
      "signature": "void StoreByteSwappedColorValue(uint colorValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Stores a byte-swapped color value to global memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load 32-bit color value from stack parameter\n2. Extract byte 0 (LSB) into CH register\n3. Extract byte 1 into EDX register\n4. Extract byte 2 (MSB) into EAX register\n5. Combine bytes: (byte1 << 16) | (byte0 << 8) | byte2\n6. Store combined value to global address 0x6fe8831c\n7. Return with stdcall cleanup\n\nParameters:\n  colorValue (uint) - 32-bit color value to byte-swap and store\n    Bit 0-7: Blue channel (byte 0)\n    Bit 8-15: Green channel (byte 1)\n    Bit 16-23: Red channel (byte 2)\n    Bit 24-31: Alpha or unused (byte 3, discarded)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; result stored at global 0x6fe8831c\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  The function implements a partial byte swap that rearranges bytes [0,1,2]\n  to [1,0,2], effectively swapping the blue and green channels while keeping\n  red in place. The high byte (byte 3) is discarded entirely.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ce76516a36316fba8a77b3056f78b031",
