      "name": "FreeVirtualMemory",
      "signature": "void FreeVirtualMemory(LPVOID pMemoryBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Deallocates a block of virtual memory using Windows VirtualFree API.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load parameter (memory pointer) from stack at [ESP + 0x4]\n2. Test if pointer is NULL\n3. If NULL, skip deallocation and return immediately\n4. If non-NULL, push three arguments onto stack:\n   - 0x8000 (MEM_RELEASE flag to release entire region)\n   - 0x0 (dwSize must be 0 when using MEM_RELEASE)\n   - EAX (pointer to memory block)\n5. Call VirtualFree at [0x6fe2c0a8]\n6. Return from function (callee-cleanup, pop return address)\n\nParameters:\n- pMemoryBlock (LPVOID): Pointer to memory block to deallocate; if NULL, function exits early without calling VirtualFree\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value; VirtualFree result is discarded\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL pointer check prevents calling VirtualFree on invalid addresses\n- Uses MEM_RELEASE (0x8000) flag to decommit and release entire allocated region\n- dwSize parameter is 0 because MEM_RELEASE requires size to be 0\n- Function is used as a cleanup wrapper, typically called from destructors or cleanup routines",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d4a2a184c05fa1794ab441d0135435ac",
