      "name": "GeneratePaletteGradient",
      "signature": "void GeneratePaletteGradient(byte * pPalette)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Generates a 256x256 palette gradient using bilinear interpolation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract 3 gradient values (CL, AL, BL) from input palette at offset +2, +0, +1\n2. Calculate normalized interpolation weights for each gradient dimension using 0x55555555\n3. Initialize output buffer at palette offset 0x5b500 with 256x256 grid\n4. For each of 256 rows:\n   a. Load current row and neighboring rows from input palette\n   b. Find max gradient value between current and neighbors using comparison logic\n   c. Calculate interpolation factor as (0xff - max_gradient)\n   d. For each of 256 columns in the row:\n      - Compute weighted average of 4 neighboring palette colors using bilinear interpolation\n      - Call FindClosestPaletteColor to map result to nearest palette index\n      - Store result in output buffer\n5. Write result to palette buffer at offset 0x6b500\n\nParameters:\npPalette - Pointer to palette buffer with color lookup table\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies palette buffer in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles zero gradient values for all three dimensions\n- Uses magic constant 0x55555555 for normalized fixed-point weight calculation\n- Uses magic constant 0x80808081 for division-by-256 optimization\n- Supports gradients along X (CL), Y (AL), and Z (BL) dimensions\n- Output grid at +0x5b500 contains 256x256 interpolated palette indices\n- Gradient lookup at +0x6b500 contains base palette data\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name          Type    Description\n0x0     400   colorLookup         byte[256] 256 base palette colors\n0x5b500 65536 gradientPalette     byte[256][256] Bilinear interpolated gradient grid\n0x6b500 256   gradientReference   byte[256] Reference gradient values",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:93f3b250869cded29fa28b7bc6157ae7",
