      "name": "ClearGlobalLRUCache",
      "signature": "void ClearGlobalLRUCache(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Clears the global LRU (Least Recently Used) cache.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EDI register (callee-saved register for preservation)\n2. Load global cache context pointer from 0x6fe872b0 into EDI\n3. Call ClearLRUCache function to clear cache contents\n4. Restore EDI register to its original state\n5. Return to caller\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function performs cache cleanup as a side effect.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Preserves EDI register per __stdcall convention\n- Uses global context pointer at 0x6fe872b0 for cache management\n- Called 11 times throughout the binary indicating frequent cache resets",
