      "name": "DestroyAllGameEntities",
      "signature": "void DestroyAllGameEntities(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Iterates through a linked list of game entities and destroys all valid entities\nwith valid context handles. For each entity in the global entity list, validates\nthe context and conditionally destroys the entity while clearing its reference.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the global entity list head pointer from DAT_6fe7725c\n2. If list is empty (NULL), exit immediately\n3. Loop through linked list nodes:\n   a. Load current node's entity pointer from offset +0x0\n   b. Verify entity pointer is non-NULL\n   c. Load entity context/handle from offset +0xb0\n   d. If context is valid, call ValidateContextAndWaitHandle()\n   e. If validation succeeds (return 0), call DestroyGameEntity()\n   f. Clear the entity context pointer at offset +0xb0 to NULL\n   g. Advance to next node via offset +0x14\n4. Return after all nodes processed\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If global list pointer (DAT_6fe7725c) is NULL, function returns immediately\n- Empty nodes (entity pointer = 0) are skipped without destruction\n- Only entities with valid context handles are destroyed\n- Offset +0xb0 holds the entity context/handle that's cleared after destruction\n- Offset +0x14 in each node points to the next node in the linked list\n- Offset +0x0 in each node contains the entity pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:015b107b956b8045d46252026c4d7b55",
