      "name": "DecompressSpriteWithCodec",
      "signature": "uint DecompressSpriteWithCodec(uint * pPixelData, int nWidth, int pSpriteConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Decompresses sprite image data using a codec decompression engine.\n\nThis function manages the sprite decompression pipeline by:\n1. Extracting codec state and base index pointers from config structure\n2. Setting decompression-in-progress flag (bit 1) in the mode word\n3. Calling the codec decompression routine with source/dest parameters\n4. Clearing decompression flag and mode flags after completion\n5. Allocating memory for decompressed sprite data\n6. Setting error flag if decompression failed\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract pCodecState from pSpriteConfig+4\n2. Extract pBaseIndex from pSpriteConfig+8\n3. Load mode word pointer from pBaseIndex+0x94\n4. Set decompression-in-progress flag (|= 2) at mode word + 0xc\n5. Call DecompressSpriteDataWithCodec with codec parameters\n6. Store decompressed data pointer at pSpriteConfig+0x14\n7. Clear decompression flag (&amp;= ~2) at mode word + 0xc\n8. Clear mode flags (&amp;= ~0x04) at pBaseIndex\n9. Allocate sprite memory for decompressed data\n10. If decompression failed (pDecompressedData == null), set error flag (|= 1) at pCodecState\n\nParameters:\n  pPixelData (uint*) - Pointer to compressed sprite pixel data buffer\n  nWidth (int) - Width parameter or stride for decompression\n  pSpriteConfig (int) - Pointer to sprite configuration structure containing:\n    +0x04: pCodecState - Codec state for decompression\n    +0x08: pBaseIndex - Base index/descriptor structure\n    +0x0c: Config parameter for decompression\n    +0x10: Config parameter for decompression\n    +0x14: Output pointer for decompressed data\n    +0x18: Memory allocation size\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Always returns 1 (success status code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Sets bit 1 in mode word during decompression to prevent concurrent access\n  - Clears bit 2 (0x04) in base index after decompression\n  - Sets bit 0 (error flag) if decompressed data is null\n  - Calls AllocateSpriteMemory regardless of decompression success",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
