      "name": "ValidateAndInitializeEntityData",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndInitializeEntityData(uint entityTypeValue, byte * pEntityData, int pEntityConfig, int param4, int param5)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates entity configuration and initializes game session state.\n\nThis function performs comprehensive validation of entity data pointers and\nconfiguration parameters, then initializes the game session based on entity type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (non-null pointers, valid indices)\n2. Extract entity type code from configuration at offset +0x8\n3. Based on entity type, determine start and end indices for data processing\n4. Calculate offset delta between end and start indices\n5. If offset delta is zero, serialize entity data and get file path\n6. If offset delta non-zero and game state flag at +0xb0 is clear:\n   a. Store byte values from entity data to game state\n   b. Build offset array from data table for range [startIndex:endIndex]\n   c. Check if flag at param2+0x4 bit 2 is set (complexity flag)\n   d. If set: initialize game session with callback handler and flag 0x4\n   e. If clear: initialize game session without callback\n   f. Validate session initialization succeeded, return error if failed\n7. On error: call GetReturnAddress with error code, CleanupAndAbort, then _exit(-1)\n\nParameters:\n  entityTypeValue (ECX): Entity class/type identifier (unused in type check)\n  pEntityData (EDX): Pointer to entity data buffer, accessed at offsets +0x14, +0x18\n  pEntityConfig (Stack): Pointer to entity configuration, fields at +0x4, +0x8, +0x40\n  minIndex (Stack): Minimum index for offset calculation\n  maxIndex (Stack): Maximum index for offset calculation and loop bounds\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: 0 on success or early validation failure, non-zero error code from\n       game session initialization if validation passed but session init failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic offsets: +0x8=entity type code, +0x40=data table pointer, +0x14=index\n  Entity type codes: 1,2,3,4,6 have specific handling, others use default\n  Error codes: 0x355 (bounds overflow), 0x357 (negative offset), 0x386 (init failed)\n  Flag checks: param2 bit 2 determines session initialization mode",
