      "name": "ValidateAndInitializeGameEntityCache",
      "signature": "void ValidateAndInitializeGameEntityCache(void * this, void * pGameState, int modeFlags, uint resourceLimit, byte * pEntityDataBuffer, LPSTR pFilePath, int validationFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Validates game entity data and initializes hash table cache for resource management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates parameter buffers (pEntityDataBuffer and pGameState non-null)\n2. Evaluates game state validity based on mode flags and configuration\n3. Checks mode flag (param1 == 0) and resource limit (param2 > 1)\n4. Calculates resource limit threshold: if entity count < 2, use 1; else divide by entity count\n5. Stores resource limit at offset +0x40 in game state\n6. Searches hash table bucket for entity cache initialization\n7. On failure, retrieves return address and calls cleanup/abort handler\n8. Validates entity data consistency and file paths\n9. Calls initialization routines based on validation flags\n\nParameters:\n- pGameState: pointer to game state structure with mode and configuration flags\n- modeFlags: control flags determining cache validation behavior (0 = normal)\n- resourceLimit: maximum resource count to manage in cache\n- pEntityDataBuffer: pointer to entity data with count at offset +0x14\n- pFilePath: path string for serialized entity data\n- validationFlags: flags controlling initialization behavior\n\nReturns:\n- void; initialization succeeds silently or triggers CleanupAndAbort on error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If entity count >= 2, performs integer division with shift to calculate limit\n- Mode value 6 with flag 2 set indicates special game state handling\n- Magic offset 0x6ad passed to error handler indicates error code location\n- DAT_6fe87f00 global flag overrides normal validation logic",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:250cc8c045e2558f6762d5ffb3f351fb",
