      "name": "EncodeRunLengthBuffer",
      "signature": "void EncodeRunLengthBuffer(char * pSourceBuffer, int * pOutputSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Encodes a 1024-byte (32x32) buffer using RLE (Run-Length Encoding) with chunking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 28-byte output buffer for encoded data\n2. Initialize loop to process 32 chunks of 32 bytes each (0x20 iterations)\n3. For each chunk:\n   a. Scan for null terminators (0x00) up to 127 bytes (0x7f limit)\n   b. If 127 null terminators found: encode as 0x7f marker byte\n   c. If fewer found: encode as [nullTermCount] [dataByteCount] [data bytes...]\n   d. Special handling: errorFlags indicate skip condition\n4. After each chunk: advance chunk pointers by 32 (0x20) bytes\n5. Calculate total output size as (final_write_pos - output_buffer_start)\n6. Store result size in pOutputSize parameter (RET 0x8 stdcall cleanup)\n\nParameters:\npSourceBuffer: char * - Pointer to 1024-byte input buffer (32x32 chunks)\npOutputSize: int * - Pointer to uint32 for encoded output size\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies *pOutputSize with encoded data size in bytes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Chunk size: 0x20 (32) bytes per iteration\n- Total chunks: 0x20 (32) iterations\n- Null term limit: 0x7f (127) maximum consecutive nulls\n- Data limit: 0x7f (127) maximum data bytes per chunk\n- Buffer total: 0x20 * 0x20 = 0x400 (1024) bytes input\n- Output size typically 28-256 bytes depending on data density\n\nStructure Layout - Input Buffer (1024 bytes):\nOffset  Size  Description\n0       32    Chunk 0 (32 bytes)\n32      32    Chunk 1 (32 bytes)\n...\n992     32    Chunk 31 (32 bytes)\n\nOutput Format per Chunk:\n- Mode 1 (all nulls): [0x7f]\n- Mode 2 (mixed): [nullCount] [dataCount] [data bytes]",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
