      "name": "InitializeGameDataGrid",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameDataGrid(int * pDataGrid, int * * ppOutputGrid, undefined4 param3, undefined4 param4, int nTypeId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes a 2D grid data structure and allocates contiguous memory for its elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input pointer pDataGrid is not NULL\n2. Check initialization flag (bit 0) at offset +0x4; abort if not set\n3. Validate grid type matches expected value or allowed default (6)\n4. Check if allocation flag (bit 1) at offset +0x4 is already set (skip if initialized)\n5. Load grid dimensions: rows from offset +0x10, columns from offset +0x14\n6. Calculate total allocation: rows * columns * 0x2c (44 bytes per element)\n7. Allocate contiguous memory block (0x3a6 bytes context)\n8. Zero-initialize allocated memory using REP STOSD/STOSB\n9. Iterate through rows * columns and update element pointers to absolute addresses\n10. Store allocated memory pointer at offset +0x18 in each element\n11. Set allocation flag (bit 1) to mark grid as initialized\n12. Store output pointer to ppOutputGrid\n\nParameters:\n- pDataGrid: Pointer to game data grid structure\n  - [+0x0] DWORD: Grid type (6 for game data, or param value)\n  - [+0x4] DWORD: Flags (bit 0=initialized, bit 1=allocated)\n  - [+0x10] DWORD: Row count\n  - [+0x14] DWORD: Column count\n  - [+0x18+] DWORD[]: Element pointers\n- ppOutputGrid: Output pointer to receive pDataGrid reference\n- param3: Reserved (unused)\n- param4: Reserved (unused)\n- nTypeId: Expected grid type (-1 for default type 6, or specific type)\n\nReturns:\nVoid (no return value; aborts with _exit(-1) on validation failure)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nTypeId=-1, allows default type 6; otherwise requires exact type match\n- Allocation flag prevents re-initialization if already called\n- Element size is 0x2c (44) bytes, calculated from access pattern\n- Total allocation includes grid structure overhead via 0x3a6 context\n- Pointer fixup converts relative offsets to absolute addresses in-place",
