      "name": "LookupTableByBitmask",
      "signature": "uint LookupTableByBitmask(uint tableIndex, uint bitmask)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Performs indexed table lookup with optional bitmask-based row selection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if bitmask parameter is zero (direct indexing mode)\n2. If bitmask is zero, use tableIndex directly to access base table at DAT_6fe2d958\n3. If bitmask is non-zero, use BSF (Bit Scan Forward) to find lowest set bit position\n4. Increment bit position by 1 to select table row\n5. Calculate final table offset as (row * 0x20) + tableIndex\n6. Return the DWORD value at computed table address\n7. Both paths return a single DWORD value via EAX and clean up stack\n\nParameters:\n  tableIndex (uint): Index into the table row (0-7, representing columns)\n  bitmask (uint): Bitmask for selecting table row; bit position determines row\n\nReturns:\n  uint: DWORD value retrieved from table at calculated offset\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If bitmask is 0, ignores bit position logic and uses direct indexing\n  - Row stride is 0x20 (32 bytes = 8 DWORDs per row)\n  - Table base address: 0x6fe2d958\n  - Bit position range determines row offset (0-31 possible from bitmask)\n  - Function uses __stdcall, callee cleans stack with RET 0x8\n\nTable Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Description\n  ------  ----  -----------\n  +0x00    4    Row 0, Column 0\n  +0x04    4    Row 0, Column 1\n  +0x20    4    Row 1, Column 0 (stride = 0x20 = 8 DWORDs)\n  +0x40    4    Row 2, Column 0\n  ",
