      "name": "CreateHashTableNodeOnNotFound",
      "signature": "void CreateHashTableNodeOnNotFound(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a new hash table node when bucket lookup fails.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x82 (130) bytes for new hash table node using AllocateMemoryWithTracking\n2. If first allocation fails, set error code 0x83 and jump to error handler\n3. Initialize allocated node with zeros for first 5 dwords (offsets 0x0-0x10)\n4. Copy three key fields from pSearchKey (in EDI) to new node:\n   - Copy EDI+0x18 to node+0x0 (field 1)\n   - Copy EDI+0x1c to node+0x4 (field 2)\n   - Copy EDI+0x14 to node+0x8 (field 3)\n5. Copy current chain head pointer (from [EBX]) to node+0x10 (next pointer)\n6. Update chain head: store new node address into [EBX] to insert at bucket head\n7. Allocate 0x8e (142) bytes for associated data using AllocateMemoryWithTracking\n8. If second allocation fails, set error code 0x8f and jump to error handler\n9. Initialize allocated data with zeros for first 2 dwords\n10. Store pSearchKey pointer (EDI) into data structure at offset 0x0\n11. Store allocated data pointer into node+0xc (field 4 of node)\n12. Return with new entry fully initialized and inserted into hash table chain\n\nParameters:\nEBX (implicit): ppBucketChain - pointer to bucket head pointer (will be updated with new node)\nEDI (implicit): pSearchKey - pointer to structure with three key fields at offsets 0x14, 0x18, 0x1c\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function initializes structures and returns, or aborts on allocation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error code 0x83: First allocation (0x82 bytes) failed\n- Error code 0x8f: Second allocation (0x8e bytes) failed\n- Allocation failures call GetReturnAddress, CleanupAndAbort, then _exit(-1)\n- New node inserted at bucket chain head (LIFO order)\n- Both allocations must succeed or function aborts entire program",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:f37f2cafe4aff25e945735badcba5ea6",
