      "name": "CleanupGlobalCriticalSection",
      "signature": "void CleanupGlobalCriticalSection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Cleans up and destroys the global critical section when shutting down.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the initialization flag from DAT_6fe87ef4\n2. Test if the flag is non-zero (critical section is initialized)\n3. If flag is zero, skip cleanup and return (critical section never created)\n4. If flag is non-zero, enter the critical section to ensure thread safety\n5. Set the flag to zero to mark critical section as destroyed\n6. Delete the critical section at DAT_6fe6fba8, releasing system resources\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Always returns successfully after cleanup or if critical section not initialized\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If critical section not initialized (flag = 0), function safely returns without error\n- Critical section must be entered before deletion to prevent race conditions\n- Function assumes DAT_6fe6fba8 points to valid CRITICAL_SECTION structure\n- Used during application shutdown to clean up thread synchronization resources",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:3bc4b403d012c66d264a2a82802842f8",
