      "name": "AllocateFromMemoryPool",
      "signature": "void AllocateFromMemoryPool(MemoryPool * pPool)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Allocates memory from a memory pool by advancing the allocation pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the remaining size field from pool structure offset +0xc\n2. Add 7 to align up to next 8-byte boundary\n3. Align the value down to 8-byte boundary (AND with 0xFFFFFFF8)\n4. Mask the aligned value to 5-bit range (0-31) and store back to offset +0xc\n5. Shift aligned value right by 5 bits (divide by 32) to get block count\n6. Multiply block count by 4 to get byte offset\n7. Add offset to the pointer field at offset +0x4\n8. Store updated pointer back to offset +0x4\n\nParameters:\n  pPool (MemoryPool*): Pointer to memory pool structure containing allocation state\n\nReturns:\n  void: No return value; modifies pool structure in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Magic number 0x7: Used to round up to next 8-byte boundary\n  - Magic number 0xfffffff8: Aligns down to 8-byte boundary\n  - Magic number 0x1f (5 bits): Masks size to 0-31 bytes\n  - Magic number 0x5: Right shift amount (divide by 32)\n  - Magic number 0x2: Left shift amount (multiply by 4)\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset | Size | Field Name     | Type  | Description\n  -------|------|----------------|-------|-------------------------------------\n  0x0    | 4    | reserved_0     | uint  | Reserved/unused field\n  0x4    | 4    | ptrOffset      | uint  | Current allocation pointer offset\n  0x8    | 4    | reserved_8     | uint  | Reserved/unused field\n  0xc    | 4    | remainingSize  | uint  | Remaining size in bytes (masked)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
