      "name": "CopyVector128",
      "signature": "void CopyVector128(undefined4 * pDestination)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Copies a 128-bit (16-byte) value from source to destination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load first dword from source pointer\n2. Store to destination+0x0\n3. Load second dword from source+0x4\n4. Store to destination+0x4\n5. Load third dword from source+0x8\n6. Store to destination+0x8\n7. Load fourth dword from source+0xC\n8. Store to destination+0xC\n9. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pDestination (ECX): Pointer to destination buffer (must be 16-byte aligned)\n  IMPLICIT: pSourceData (EAX): Pointer to source buffer (must be 16-byte aligned)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  This is a high-performance 128-bit copy function typically used for copying vector/SIMD data or aligned structures. Source pointer is passed implicitly in EAX register, characteristic of optimized data copy routines.",
