      "name": "AllocateAndInitializeStructure",
      "signature": "void * AllocateAndInitializeStructure(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a 42-byte structure from game context.\n\nThis function allocates a block of memory, zeroes it completely, and then\ninitializes it by iterating over a context object's data. If the context\npointer (in ESI) is invalid or allocation fails, the function terminates\nthe program with error codes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 42 bytes (0x2a) of memory using AllocateMemoryWithTracking\n2. If allocation fails, retrieve return address and abort with error code 0x2b\n3. Zero-initialize entire allocated block (0x80 dwords = 512 bytes)\n4. Validate that context pointer in ESI is non-null\n5. If context is null, abort with error code 0x3ba\n6. Initialize structure by calling FUN_6fe22f20 once per count in context\n7. Context count stored at offset +0x10c (typically player/unit count)\n8. Return pointer to initialized structure\n\nParameters:\n- ESI (Implicit): Context pointer (game state, player list, or entity manager)\n  Contains a count field at offset +0x10c\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Pointer to allocated and initialized 42-byte structure\n- Program termination on allocation or context validation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Allocation size is always 42 bytes (0x2a) regardless of use\n- Zero-initialization loop processes 128 dwords (512 bytes) for 42-byte struct\n- ESI context is implicit parameter, not function argument\n- Calling code at Ordinal_10003 must provide valid context in ESI\n- Function calls _exit(-1) on error, never returns to caller\n\nImplicit Parameters:\n- ESI: Game context/entity manager with count at offset +0x10c",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
