      "name": "ClearMemoryBuffer64KB",
      "signature": "void ClearMemoryBuffer64KB(void * pBuffer, uint dwReserved)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Clears a 64KB memory buffer to zero using optimized REP STOSD instruction.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save EDI register (callee-save)\n2. Initialize counter ECX to 0x4000 (16,384 dwords)\n3. Clear EAX register (store value of 0)\n4. Load destination pointer to EDI\n5. Execute REP STOSD to write 0 to 16,384 consecutive dwords\n6. Restore EDI register\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n  pBuffer: Pointer to the 64KB memory buffer to clear (fastcall: EDX)\n  dwReserved: Reserved parameter, not used in function (fastcall: ECX)\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function clears memory in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Clears exactly 64KB (0x4000 * 4 bytes)\n  - Uses optimized REP STOSD for maximum performance\n  - Preserves all registers except EDI (saved/restored)\n  - Assumes 32-bit dword operations (assumes x86 architecture)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:adca87c70f77ad739a3a9fcfb7bbeaa1",
