      "name": "MultiplyLargeNumbersWithValidation",
      "signature": "void MultiplyLargeNumbersWithValidation(uint * pResult, uint * pMultiplier)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Multiplies two 96-bit large numbers with full validation and normalization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load and validate input operands: extract exponents/signs from offset +10\n2. XOR input signs to compute output sign bit (0x8000 mask)\n3. Validate both exponents < 0x7fff and sum < 0xbffe (prevent overflow)\n4. Check exponent sum >= 0x3fc0 (minimum magnitude threshold)\n5. Handle zero operands: if either has zero mantissa, return zero result\n6. Initialize 96-bit result accumulator (12 bytes at stack offset -0xc)\n7. Execute nested multiplication loop: 5 outer iterations \u00d7 5 inner iterations\n   a. For each outer iteration i (0-4): multiply result[i] by all multiplier words\n   b. Inner loop: multiply pMultiplier[j] by pResult[i], add to accumulator[i+j]\n   c. Propagate carries through accumulator words during multiplication\n8. Add exponent bias (0xc002) and perform normalization\n9. Normalize result by shifting mantissa left/right based on exponent\n   a. If exponent < 1: right-shift mantissa, accumulate rounding bit\n   b. If exponent > 0: left-shift mantissa until MSB set or exponent = 1\n   c. Track rounding bit (set if any bits shifted out right)\n10. Round result if rounding bit was set (set LSB of mantissa)\n11. Validate result words don't overflow all-ones pattern (0xffffffff)\n12. Write normalized result words back to pResult at offsets 0, 2, 6\n13. Apply sign bit (0x8000) to exponent and store at offset +10\n14. Check final exponent: if >= 0x7fff, set result to infinity\n\nParameters:\npResult: [EBP+0x8] = pointer to 96-bit large number (12 bytes)\n  Offset 0-1: low word of mantissa\n  Offset 2-5: middle 32 bits of mantissa\n  Offset 6-9: high 32 bits with MSB at offset 10 bit 15\n  Offset 10-11: exponent (15 bits) and sign bit (bit 15=0x8000)\npMultiplier: [EBP+0xc] = pointer to 96-bit large number (same format)\n\nReturns: void; result written to pResult in-place with normalized mantissa and exponent\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Zero result: if either operand has zero mantissa (all words = 0)\n- Minimum magnitude: if exponent sum < 0x3fc0, result is zero\n- Infinity: if exponent sum >= 0x7fff, result is infinity with sign bit preserved\n- Rounding: mantissa rounded up if any bits shifted out during normalization\n- Overflow detection: if rounded mantissa overflows, increment exponent and check again\n\nStack Usage: 0x30 bytes (48 decimal) for local variables and alignment",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
