      "name": "UnwindExceptionHandler",
      "signature": "void UnwindExceptionHandler(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Exception unwinding handler that unlinks the current exception frame from the chain.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load exception frame node pointer from EBP + 0xC (caller's stack frame parameter)\n2. Push pointer onto stack as parameter\n3. Call UnlinkExceptionFrameNode to remove frame from exception handler chain\n4. Return to caller with stack frame cleaned up\n\nParameters:\n  pExceptionFrameNode - Pointer to exception frame node structure containing linked list\n                       pointers for exception handler chain management\n\nReturns:\n  void - Uses __stdcall calling convention (callee cleans 4-byte parameter)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Part of C++ exception handling mechanism (likely compiler-generated)\n  - Called from 17 different exception handler functions via function pointer table\n  - References to this function are stored in data sections, indicating it's dispatched\n    through function pointer arrays rather than direct calls\n  - Must maintain SEH (Structured Exception Handling) chain integrity on x86\n\nNote:\n  This is a thin wrapper around UnlinkExceptionFrameNode that marshals parameters\n  from the stack. The actual exception frame unlinking logic is in the called function.",
